<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="TransitLab.Views.RevisionHistoryView">

    <ScrollViewer HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                  VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">

        <StackPanel Spacing="6" Margin="32,20,32,24">

            <!-- ── v2.10.0 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.10.0  —  2026-09-03" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: the MObs tab no longer queries MicroObservatory's own servers directly. TransitLab's growing user base was putting real load on MicroObservatory's infrastructure, so a separate daily sync job now mirrors the Cecilia telescope's recent FITS data to a Cloudflare-hosted cache once each morning, and every TransitLab install reads from that shared cache instead. The trade-off: data refreshes once daily rather than live, so a frame from a session that just finished won't show up until the next day's sync — not an issue for normal next-day analysis, but worth knowing if you're checking right after an overnight run. Fetch List, Download Selected, and Use This Data all work exactly as before; only where the data comes from has changed. Lookback days now maxes out at 14 (previously 30), matching how far back the daily sync actually mirrors." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix (issue #47): the MObs observations list's column headers could appear cut off before any Fetch List had been run. The Weather column used star ('*') width sizing to fill the grid's remaining space, but Avalonia's DataGrid only resolves star-column widths against actual row content — with zero rows, the calculation collapsed and clipped the header. Weather now uses a fixed width like the other columns, so the header row is always sized correctly regardless of whether the list is empty." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix (issue #47): the Object column in the MObs observations list could truncate longer target names (e.g. all-caps/digit-heavy names like 'WASP-77A'). The list already auto-sizes that column (and Date, Science Frames, Cal Frames) from the actual fetched content each time Fetch List runs, but the underlying per-character width estimate was too tight for the real rendered font. Widened the estimate to give every column comfortable headroom." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix (issue #43): selecting a row in the MObs observations list could make the whole Data tab jump — the list would slide up and cover the Directories panel above it. The list had no maximum height, so it grew to fit every fetched observation and relied on the tab's own outer scroll area for scrolling; selecting a row shifted keyboard focus into the list, and Avalonia's default focus-follow behavior scrolled the entire tab so the list's top edge landed at the top of the visible area, hiding everything above it. The list now has a capped height and scrolls its own rows internally, so selecting a row no longer moves the rest of the tab." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #49): Fetch from NEA (Equipment &amp; Target tab) now falls back to NextAstro's cached mirror of NASA Exoplanet Archive parameters if the live archive is unreachable — a connection failure, timeout, or outage — instead of failing outright. This mirrors a fallback EXOTIC's own pre-release build already uses internally during a run. The status line and session log note when data came from the NextAstro cache rather than the live archive, so it's clear which source was used." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #48): Quick Look button (top bar, next to Save &amp; Run EXOTIC) — runs a fast least-squares fit instead of EXOTIC's full ultranest posterior inference, for a quick preliminary look at a light curve. Reuses the exact same field validation, inits.json, and FITS directories as a normal run — only the mode passed to EXOTIC differs. No AAVSO report is produced, so Submit Results on the Results tab stays disabled with an explanation, and a preliminary banner appears while/after a Quick Look run. Requires the EXOTIC 4.3.2 pre-release dev build — greyed out otherwise, with a [?] explaining why." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #48): Advanced settings (Tools → Settings → Advanced) exposing five more EXOTIC 4.3.2 pre-release-only options, each with a [?] explanation: Non-interactive run (auto-resolves invalid RA/Dec and unrecognized limb-darkening filter prompts instead of pausing for input), NextAstro variability server (batch comparison-star variability check instead of one-by-one VSX lookups, with automatic VSX fallback on error), Multiprocessing process counts for frame alignment and light-curve fitting (blank = today's single-process behavior), Use ensemble photometry (combines multiple comparison stars into one median-normalized reference instead of EXOTIC picking a single best-fitting comp star — default On), and Use exactly the comps provided (uses every comp star TransitLab's Stone selection vetted instead of EXOTIC re-ranking and capping to its own top 5 — default On, since Stone already does its own thorough vetting including a VSX variability cross-check). All five can be turned on regardless of which EXOTIC environment is active — TransitLab only actually sends them to EXOTIC when the pre-release build is the one running, so they're silently ignored otherwise rather than needing to be re-toggled per environment." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: a one-time popup the first time TransitLab detects the EXOTIC 4.3.2 pre-release dev build is active, introducing Quick Look and the five Advanced settings above so they don't go unnoticed." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: MObs downloads now log per-file diagnostics — byte size, elapsed time, effective speed, and (on success) the Cloudflare CF-RAY value that proves the file was actually served from R2 rather than somewhere else. A per-batch summary line (total time, succeeded/failed counts) is added after every download. Previously a failed file was silently counted with no log entry explaining why; failures now log the actual exception type and message." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: [?] explanations for the Frame alignment and Light-curve fits process-count fields in Advanced settings, matching every other option there." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: many buttons throughout the app showed their label off-center rather than centered. Avalonia's Button defaults to stretching its content rather than centering it, so any button wider than its own text — from a fixed minimum width, or from being stretched across a layout column — rendered its label left-aligned instead of centered. Centering is now set once at the app level, so every button is affected, not just ones fixed individually. A few buttons had also been manually padded with extra leading/trailing spaces in their label text as a workaround; removed, since proper centering makes that unnecessary and the manual spacing wasn't even symmetric." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: standardized the size of every plain 'OK' button used throughout the app's [?] help popups and info dialogs — previously a fairly generous fixed minimum width for a two-letter label, now a more proportionate size. Cancel/Save/Proceed-style buttons with longer labels are unaffected." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: the MObs section on the Data tab now states its once-daily refresh schedule directly (13:00 UTC), matching the same detail already covered in the User Guide and the [?] help popup." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the MObs observations list could look like it was silently dropping results — e.g. showing only 9 rows after Fetch List reported '28 observations found.' All 28 were actually there; the list's height is capped so it scrolls its own rows internally (see the v2.9.1 fix above for the list jumping on row-select), but the scrollbar for that was a thin overlay that auto-hides, easy to miss entirely against the dark theme. The scrollbar is now always visible, so it's obvious there's more to scroll to." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Lookback Days on the MObs tab could silently exclude a session from as recently as 'yesterday,' depending what time of day Fetch List was clicked — e.g. Lookback Days = 1 could miss a session from the previous UTC day entirely, needing 2 to show it. The cutoff was computed as 'right now minus N days,' which carries today's current time-of-day, but observation dates are date-only (always midnight) — so a fetch made anytime after midnight UTC compared yesterday's midnight against a cutoff later than midnight, excluding it. Lookback Days now correctly counts back from the start of today, not the current moment." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: StarFix — a separate, first-party plate-solving app (ArtTrail/StarFix) with its own offline Gaia DR3 catalog — added as a solver option in Plate Solve Setup, now listed first, and fully wired up. Selecting it shows a setup panel with a Download &amp; Install button that fetches the latest StarFix installer and launches it (the install wizard itself is StarFix's own — TransitLab doesn't manage the Gaia catalog download, that stays inside StarFix). Auto-detects an existing install via its Windows uninstall registry entry, since the installer lets you choose any install location. Solving (single frame or Solve All Frames) invokes StarFix's own headless solve tool directly and writes the WCS into the FITS file in place, the same as ASTAP — verified against a real MObs frame before shipping (48/51 stars matched, 1.78px RMS) — the direct answer to issue #40 (ASTAP's persistent failure on MObs' small image frames), though that issue is left open until this ships in a release, since ASTAP itself is unchanged." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: reordered the plate solver list to StarFix, ASTAP, NextAstro, Astrometry.net, and removed 'experimental' from the NextAstro description." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Solve All Frames (any solver — StarFix, ASTAP, Astrometry.net, or NextAstro) attempted every FITS file physically present in the directory, with no awareness of frames checked 'Excl' in Image Analysis. Those solvers list the FITS folder directly rather than going through Image Analysis' frame list, so an excluded frame — a trail, a dark, a bad exposure — could still be sent to the solver and waste a solve attempt (or, worse, succeed with a bogus WCS). Solve All Frames now filters out every currently-excluded path before solving, for all four solvers." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix (issue #50): locating the ASTAP executable on Linux/macOS was unreliable — the file picker's named filter (matching exact binary names like 'astap'/'astap_cli') is now secondary to an 'All files' default on those platforms, since there's no single guaranteed binary name across distros, source builds, and AppImages the way there is on Windows. The install-path field's watermark text no longer says '.exe' on Linux/macOS. Also: if the selected ASTAP binary is missing its executable permission (common after extracting a downloaded archive, since that bit often isn't preserved), TransitLab now sets it automatically before launching ASTAP, and reports a clear chmod-related message if that still fails, instead of a bare 'Permission denied.'" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #9): Windows Inno Setup installer — an additional way to get TransitLab on Windows, alongside the existing portable win-x64 zip (which still works exactly as before). Installs per-user into %LocalAppData%\TransitLab, no admin/UAC required; the separate %AppData%\TransitLab folder holding config.json, history.json, and session logs is untouched by install or uninstall." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: self-updating. When a new version is available and TransitLab detects it's running from an Inno-installed copy (not the portable zip), the update banner offers 'Update Now' alongside the existing manual 'Download' option — it downloads the new installer and runs it silently, which closes TransitLab, reinstalls in place, and reopens it automatically, with no manual extraction or file replacement needed. Portable-zip installs, and Mac/Linux (no Inno installer exists for those platforms), keep the existing manual download-and-extract flow unchanged." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: TransitLab now also checks for updates once a day (00:00 UTC, within a 30-minute window) while running, not just at launch — for anyone who leaves it open for long observing sessions rather than relaunching daily. Clicking Skip on the update banner now means 'don't ask about this specific version again' — it's remembered across both the daily re-check and future relaunches — rather than reappearing on the very next check. The manual Check for Updates command (Help menu) always reports the true current status regardless of anything previously skipped." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Help → Previous Versions could show a non-app entry (e.g. 'gaia-catalog-v1' — data hosted on this same GitHub repo for an unrelated project, StarFix's Gaia catalog) mixed in with real TransitLab versions. More seriously, the update checker and self-update both ask GitHub for the repo's 'latest' release, which resolves to whatever was published most recently regardless of what it actually is — since that non-app release is newer than the last real TransitLab version, both were unknowingly asking the wrong release for its version number (harmless so far only by accident: a non-numeric tag fails to parse as a version, so no incorrect update banner ever appeared). All three now specifically look for a real 'vX.Y.Z'-style TransitLab version tag rather than trusting whatever 'latest' happens to mean." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: User Guide reformatted to match StarFix's guide — a title heading at the top, and a floating ↑ 'back to top' button (bottom-right) that stays visible while scrolling. Added a References section at the end listing the software, services, and published sources TransitLab relies on or integrates with (EXOTIC, NASA Exoplanet Archive, AAVSO, Gaia DR3, APASS, Geoffrey Stone's CompStarSelector, ASTAP, Astrometry.net, StarFix, MicroObservatory, and the Visualizer/filter-defaults papers already cited inline elsewhere in the guide), with a new Table of Contents entry pointing to it." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: nextastro.org link added under the NextAstro option in Plate Solve Setup, matching the existing hnsky.org/astap.htm link under ASTAP." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the StarFix line in Plate Solve Setup's solver list (the longest of the four) didn't wrap to a second line on a narrower window — it was set via RadioButton's plain Content string, which doesn't wrap by default, while NextAstro already used a wrapping TextBlock instead. StarFix, ASTAP, and Astrometry.net now all use the same wrapping TextBlock as NextAstro, so every solver description wraps consistently regardless of window width." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: the StarFix line in Plate Solve Setup no longer says 'no internet required once installed' (just 'no internet required' — matching how ASTAP's own line is worded); a github.com/ArtTrail/StarFix link was added underneath it, matching the nextastro.org/hnsky.org links already under NextAstro/ASTAP." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: Help → About reformatted to match StarFix's About window — the TransitLab app icon now appears at the top, the GitHub link moved from a standalone button near the top to a plain line under the Author section (alongside email), and a License section was added at the bottom referencing the included LICENSE file. The Acknowledgements list itself is unchanged content-wise, aside from adding the Exoplanet Slacker site link under Douglas James's existing credit." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: in the User Guide's search, jumping to a match anywhere in the document scrolled 'Find Next' itself out of view along with everything else, since the title and search bar lived inside the same scrolling content as the guide text — reaching the next match required manually scrolling back up first. The title and search bar are now a fixed header above the scrolling guide content, so they stay reachable no matter where a match lands." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Find Next now highlights the matched text itself, not just the paragraph it's in — previously it only scrolled the match into view with no indication of where in that paragraph it actually was. The highlight moves to the next match (or clears entirely on Clear or a new search) rather than stacking up." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Help → About sized itself to fit all of its content unconditionally (SizeToContent, no cap) — with the logo, Acknowledgements, and License now added, it could ask for a window taller than a smaller screen's own working area, with no way to see the rest. It now defaults to about 2/3 of the current screen's height and scrolls internally for anything that doesn't fit, and can be resized (previously fixed-size) if you want it taller or shorter." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: the StarFix link in Plate Solve Setup now points to github.com/ArtTrail/StarFix/releases/latest instead of the repo root, so it opens straight to the current downloadable release rather than the repo's front page." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Fetch from NEA failed for HAT-P-10 and HAT-P-71 — both are indexed in NASA's archive only under a different host-star name (WASP-11 and WASP-194 respectively; confirmed directly against NEA's own alias-lookup service, not assumed), so a query for the HAT-P name itself returned nothing. These two specific cases are now recognized and silently redirected to the name NEA actually has data under, updating the Planet Name field to match so the rest of the run (inits.json, AAVSO submission) stays consistent with what NEA and AAVSO recognize." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: AAVSO VSP comp star fetch, the VSP chart, and VSX cross-checking could all fail with a bare 403 Forbidden — traced to www.aavso.org (the host every one of these queries used) now sitting behind a Cloudflare bot challenge that blocks any non-browser HTTP client outright, confirmed directly by testing curl and .NET's own HttpClient against the plain www.aavso.org homepage (also 403, regardless of headers). apps.aavso.org and vsx.aavso.org are separate hosts with no such challenge — confirmed serving real data to the same non-browser clients that www.aavso.org blocks — so every query now targets those instead." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.9.0 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.9.0  —  2026-08-21" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: automatic one-shot-color (OSC) camera detection. As soon as a Lights, Darks, Flats, or Biases directory is loaded, TransitLab checks the FITS header for a Bayer pattern (BAYERPAT) — the signature of raw color-camera data (e.g. Unistellar eVscope frames). If found, a prompt offers to debayer the affected directories before anything else touches the pixels, since running Image Analysis, Plate Solve, or the Stone comp method on raw mosaic data distorts star detection and photometry. Debayering runs green-channel-only bilinear demosaicing (via the same colour_demosaicing library EXOTIC itself depends on) and writes the result to a sibling Debayered folder — original raw files are never modified. TransitLab automatically switches to the debayered files and re-scans frames afterward. A progress bar and per-file status (e.g. '3 of 12…') are shown on the Data tab for the duration, rather than running silently." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: once a directory triggered the OSC prompt, it was marked as handled immediately — even if the user clicked Skip, or debayering failed — so re-selecting that same directory later in the same session silently stopped detecting it at all. Now a directory is only marked handled after debayering actually succeeds for it; declining the prompt or a failed debayer both leave it eligible to be detected and prompted again." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the plate-solve pixel-scale auto-correction message pointed to a 'Tools → Settings → Solvers' menu that doesn't exist, and instructed the user to manually save a value that is already persisted automatically the next time TransitLab closes. Simplified to just report the correction, with no action needed from the user. The same stale menu reference was also corrected in two Plate Solve log messages to the real location, Tools → Plate Solve Setup." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Solve All Frames now works with Astrometry.net and NextAstro, not just ASTAP — each frame is solved individually and written back, with a running solved/failed count, exactly like ASTAP's existing all-frames mode. Since each frame is a separate network round-trip to a hosted solver rather than an instant local solve, selecting Solve All Frames together with either online solver shows a one-time warning that a full directory can take a while." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Extended: the ASTAP struggle-warning (v2.8.3, originally MicroObservatory-only) now also covers Unistellar eVscope data, detected directly from the FITS header (ORIGIN/TELESCOP) rather than the folder it came from. This was confirmed with real testing, not assumed: even after debayering a real eVscope frame with a correct, empirically-measured pixel scale, ASTAP still failed to find a solution across a full FOV sweep, while Astrometry.net solved the identical file on the first attempt — pointing to the scope's own field distortion rather than image quality or scale as the cause. The warning text now explains this per source rather than always mentioning MObs specifically." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Solve ALL images was only visible in Plate Solve Setup while ASTAP was selected — it sat inside the ASTAP-only settings panel from before Solve All Frames worked with every solver, so switching to Astrometry.net or NextAstro hid the checkbox entirely. Moved to its own always-visible section beneath the solver-specific settings." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the 'Solving All Frames May Take a While' warning could appear when selecting ASTAP or NextAstro, regardless of which solver was actually chosen, because the check ran on every radio-button change rather than only when an online solver was actively being selected. Now only fires when Astrometry.net or NextAstro is turned on (directly, or via Solve All Frames being checked while one is already active) — never as a side effect of switching to a different solver." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #41): Pop Out button on the Image Analysis tab's image viewer (next to Auto Stretch), for laptop and small-screen users. Opens the full image viewer — zoom, pan, pixel/ADU cursor readout, target/comp-star picking, Black/White stretch sliders, Auto Stretch, marker overlays — in its own separate, resizable window. The frame list stays in the main window so a different frame can still be selected while looking at the bigger popped-out view; picks, stretch, and zoom stay in sync either way. Closing the pop-out window (its own X button or the in-panel Bring Back button) restores it to the tab." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: the Pre-release / Development Build environment now detects and installs its own Python 3.12 base interpreter, entirely independent of Stable's Python 3.10. Some EXOTIC branches now declare Requires-Python &gt;=3.12 in their own package metadata, which the shared Stable-oriented Python 3.10.11 interpreter can't satisfy — installing from such a branch failed immediately with 'Package exotic requires a different Python: 3.10.11 not in &gt;=3.12'. The Pre-release card now has its own Check System / Download &amp; Install Python 3.12 controls, separate from Stable's row above the two cards; Stable's own Python 3.10 detection and install is completely unchanged." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: installing a Pre-release branch could keep silently reusing an existing Pre-release environment built from an older, no-longer-sufficient Python — even right after correctly detecting and installing Python 3.12 — because the environment was only rebuilt when it didn't already exist at all, never re-checked against the current minimum version. TransitLab now checks the existing environment's own Python version before reusing it, and automatically rebuilds it fresh from the current base interpreter if it no longer meets the requirement (≥3.12 for Pre-release)." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: AAVSO submissions silently stopped appearing in the History tab again, and two related AAVSO output post-processing steps (stripping EXOTIC's invalid #SECONDARY_OBSCODES count-prefix, and generating the WebObs 2.0-safe rounded copy of the AID file) silently stopped doing anything. All three looked for EXOTIC's output files (AAVSO_*.txt, AID_AAVSO_*.txt, FinalParams_*.json) directly in a specific folder rather than searching for them, and a newer EXOTIC build moved these files into a new AAVSO_Files subfolder — so all three searches quietly found nothing every time, with no error shown anywhere. Rather than chasing the exact folder name again next time EXOTIC's own layout changes, all three now search recursively through the whole run output folder and use whichever matching file was written most recently." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.8.3 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.8.3  —  2026-08-17" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: TransitLab could crash immediately on launch, before the window ever appeared, if a saved Camera Type, Binning, Filter, or Comp Star Method setting didn't match any entry in that field's dropdown list — a corrupted config, or a value left over from a version whose list has since changed. Restoring it during startup passed a null value into code written to assume one of the dropdown's fixed options; for Filter specifically, that meant an unguarded dictionary lookup that threw outright, crashing every single launch until the saved config was fixed by hand. All four settings now fall back to a safe default if the saved value can't be matched, and Filter's own change handler no longer assumes a non-null value regardless of how it got there. Diagnosed from a live user's exported Windows Event Viewer logs, which pinpointed the exact crash and its origin in the startup config-restore path — a case that looked at first like a Windows security block, since the app never got far enough to show any error dialog at all." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix (issue #39): Plate Solve could keep re-solving a frame that had since been excluded in Image Analysis, if the plate solver was switched (or re-run) after Read FITS Header had already cached that frame as the solve target. The cached path was only refreshed when empty, not re-checked against the current exclusion list, so a newly-excluded frame silently kept being targeted until Read FITS Header was clicked again. Plate Solve now always re-derives the current first-non-excluded frame before solving, falling back to the cached path only if that lookup is unavailable." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: warning popup when plate solving MicroObservatory (MObs) data with ASTAP selected. ASTAP can struggle with MObs' small image frames, sometimes failing outright or solving incorrectly. Detected directly from the FITS file being solved (OBSERVAT='Whipple Observatory' / TELESCOP matching one of MObs' four telescopes) rather than how the folder was loaded, so it fires even for MObs data reached by manually browsing to it rather than via the MObs tab. The popup recommends switching to Astrometry.net (EXOTIC 4.3.1) or NextAstro (EXOTIC 4.3.2 pre-release) instead, and appears each time a solve is attempted under these conditions rather than blocking it." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.8.2 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.8.2  —  2026-08-13" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: FITS frames with a .fts extension (the classic 8.3-filename-era alternate for .fits — same file format, just a shorter suffix) were invisible to Scan Frames and several other file-discovery paths, even though TransitLab could read the format perfectly well once pointed at one directly. Added .fts alongside .fits/.fit/.fz to Scan Frames, the dark-frame directory scan, plate-solve file discovery, and Read FITS Header's candidate-file fallback." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Check Version button in the Pre-release card of Python &amp; EXOTIC Setup. With Pre-release selected (●) and a branch URL entered, resolves the exact version that branch would install right now — via a pip dry-run, so nothing is actually installed — and compares it against what's currently installed, reporting either 'up to date', 'new version available' with both full version strings shown, or the branch's current version if nothing is installed yet. No reinstall needed just to check." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the installed-version line in Python &amp; EXOTIC Setup (Stable and Pre-release cards) could run off the edge of the window instead of wrapping to a second line, most visible with the longer dev-build version strings. TextWrapping was already set, but the line sat inside a horizontally-stacked layout that measures its children at unconstrained width, so wrapping never actually had room to kick in — switched to a layout that properly constrains the text column's width." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Download &amp; Install Python (used when no compatible Python is detected) silently prepended the newly-installed Python 3.10.11 to the system-wide PATH environment variable — meaning 'python'/'pip' typed in any terminal, anywhere on the machine, would resolve to this install first, ahead of whatever the user already had (their own venvs, IDE configs, other tools). TransitLab never actually needed this: every caller already resolves this interpreter by its known fixed install path, never by a bare PATH lookup. Python 3.10.11 now installs cleanly side-by-side with zero footprint on the rest of the system." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.8.1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.8.1  —  2026-08-10" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: comparison-star fetches (both AAVSO VSP and Stone / VSP + Stone) could silently accept catalog positions that don't actually correspond to a detectable star in the image — a chart or Gaia/APASS entry only guarantees a star exists at that RA/Dec on paper, not that it's bright enough to measure in this exposure. On a faint target/field, this could mean some or even all of the 'comparison stars' were actually just blank sky, producing a light curve dominated by noise with no indication anything was wrong (traced back to two independent real cases). Both methods now measure each candidate against the actual FITS pixel data before accepting it: AAVSO VSP drops any candidate with no real detectable signal and tries the next chart candidate instead; Stone / VSP + Stone tracks whether the final comp stars actually cleared the PSF/SNR quality bar rather than just reporting whatever was left after the backfill pool ran dry. When every candidate fails — for AAVSO VSP, or when Stone's final selection never validated a single star — the status now shows an explicit yellow warning instead of a plain green checkmark, and the success sound no longer plays for that case." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Read FITS Header only correctly handled site latitude/longitude when the header already stored a plain decimal degree value (e.g. MObs' convention). A sexagesimal degrees-minutes-seconds value with a trailing hemisphere letter instead of a sign (e.g. SITELAT='28 17 58.8 S', as used by Teide Observatory's FITS convention) was never converted to decimal at all, and the trailing letter was ignored — so a Southern/Western site could be silently read in as positive. A leading-sign DMS value (e.g. '+28 17 58.8') kept the correct sign but was still never converted from DMS to decimal, reaching EXOTIC as unparseable text rather than a number. Both Latitude and Longitude are now converted from any of these formats (plain decimal, leading-sign DMS, or DMS with a trailing N/S/E/W letter) to a correct signed decimal value when the header is read, and Save &amp; Run's pre-flight validation now checks that these fields actually parse as numbers instead of only checking they're non-blank. A follow-up fix corrected a regression from this same change: unsigned positive values (e.g. MObs' plain 'LATITUDE=31.68', with no '+') were being passed to EXOTIC without a leading sign at all, which EXOTIC's own input validation rejects outright ('You forgot the sign for the latitude!') — a Northern/Eastern site with no sign in the header could silently hit this error every run. Both fields now always carry an explicit leading '+' or '-'." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the History tab silently stopped gaining new rows after a successful AAVSO submission. Recording a submission looked up that run's FinalParams_*.json using the live Save Plots directory field, but that field is reset back to the base directory as soon as a run finishes — the actual file lives inside that run's own per-run output subfolder (introduced in v2.8.0), so the lookup found nothing and quietly gave up every time, with no error shown. Now derives the correct folder from the report path the Results tab already resolved when it verified the upload, instead of the (by-then-stale) Save Plots directory field." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: an Astrometry.net or NextAstro plate solve could fail outright with a bare 'No such file or directory' error pointing at a working_artifacts\wcs.fits path, on EXOTIC builds that save the solved WCS file to a working_artifacts subfolder instead of temp. TransitLab's plate-solve helper already creates the save directory's temp subfolder before handing off to EXOTIC, but had no reason to also create working_artifacts — a folder some EXOTIC builds expect to already exist and never create themselves. The helper now pre-creates both, so the solve no longer depends on which convention the active EXOTIC build happens to use." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: NextAstro could stay greyed out in Plate Solve Setup even with the required EXOTIC 4.3.2 pre-release dev build installed and selected. The version check used a generic system-Python lookup that predates v2.8.0's separate Stable/Pre-release environments, so it frequently found Stable's plain '4.3.2' instead of Pre-release's '4.3.2.dev…' regardless of which environment was actually active. The check now queries whichever environment is currently selected in Setup — the same resolution already used for naming Results folders and launching EXOTIC itself." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Removed: Auto Select Comps. This button scanned the FITS image and picked comparison stars purely by matching peak ADU brightness to the target, with no astrometric or photometric quality checks — a much cruder approach than the Stone comp star pipeline, which scores candidates on color similarity, magnitude match, flux SNR, RUWE astrometric quality, and field centrality, with PSF validation. Removed from the Parameters tab, the automation sequence, User Guide, and Quick Start, along with its underlying ADU-based star-detection code." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Comp Star Details could show a green checkmark in the PSF column for a comp star that had actually failed PSF validation. The per-star status only checked for saturation and whether a measurement existed at all — it never checked the star's SNR against the same 75-point floor the validation pipeline itself uses, so a star that was measured but fell well short of that floor (e.g. SNR of 4–13, only kept because the entire candidate pool ran dry) still showed a plain ✓, contradicting the correct 'poor' grade and warning already shown just above the table. Added a new ⚠ Low SNR status for this case, and corrected the column's help text, which still described a '⚠ PSF' label retired back in v2.7.0." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the Install / Reinstall button in Python &amp; EXOTIC Setup stayed disabled after every restart, even when Stable and/or Pre-release already showed as fully installed — it only became usable after clicking Check System at least once in that session. The base Python path used to create a new environment is a session-only value that was never restored from the saved config on launch (unlike each environment's own python.exe path, which is), so the button's enabled state silently depended on a Check System click that most users had no reason to make. This also blocked the most direct way to update an already-installed Pre-release build from the same GitHub branch URL without uninstalling first — Install / Reinstall already reuses the existing environment and branch URL history for exactly that, it just couldn't be clicked. Now restored from the saved config on launch, so both buttons are usable immediately." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: the Install / Reinstall, Uninstall, and Remove buttons in Python &amp; EXOTIC Setup had no description of what they actually do, and their names invited confusion — Uninstall and Remove sound interchangeable but aren't. Added a hover tooltip to each of the six buttons, and a new [?] help button next to the EXOTIC Environments header explaining all three: Install / Reinstall creates the environment if needed and (re)installs EXOTIC into it in place; Uninstall removes only the EXOTIC package and keeps the environment itself; Remove deletes the whole environment outright, including Python itself, and has to be rebuilt from scratch on the next install." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: a run could exit with EXOTIC's own '✓ finished successfully' message while producing no report, light curve, or fitted parameters whatsoever — most commonly on a very faint field/exposure where TransitLab's own comp-star grading already warns 'poor'. EXOTIC has a require_comp_star safeguard (on by default) that aborts the fit outright, with exit code 0, if literally every comparison-star candidate fails its own internal photometry check — silently indistinguishable from a genuine success by exit code alone. TransitLab now checks that a run actually produced a report, light curve, or parameters file before calling it a success, and if not, reads the real reason from that run's own EXOTIC_RunLog_*.log (a separate internal debug log EXOTIC never prints to the console, so this reason was previously invisible anywhere in TransitLab)." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the Stable / Pre-release radio buttons in Python &amp; EXOTIC Setup could fail to show which environment was actually active when the window was opened, even though the correct environment was already running behind the scenes. Both radio buttons were bound to their own independent property and also shared an Avalonia GroupName for native mutual exclusivity — but TransitLab's own view model already fully enforces that same mutual exclusivity itself, and the two mechanisms could disagree during the window's initial layout. Removed the redundant GroupName; the view model's existing logic is now the only thing deciding which one shows checked." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: a crashed run on the Pre-release build showed only '✗ EXOTIC exited with code 1' with no way to see why — the 'Detailed error log' pointer only ever checked for exotic.log, which is exclusively the Stable build's convention; Pre-release writes to a separate Diagnostics\EXOTIC_RunLog_*.log that was never checked. TransitLab now looks in both locations for any exit code, and prints the real underlying error line directly in the Results log — either an explicit EXOTIC-reported reason, or, for an unhandled Python exception, the traceback's own final 'SomeException: message' line — instead of leaving only a bare exit code and, at best, a path to a large log file to search through by hand." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Reverted: require_comp_star. Earlier in this version's development, TransitLab briefly set this to 'n' so EXOTIC would always attempt a fit rather than refuse outright on a marginal comparison-star selection. Live testing found a real bug in the Pre-release build's own code specifically in that path: when require_comp_star is off, EXOTIC adds a 'fit with no comparison star at all' candidate into its scoring, and if that candidate wins the scoring competition on a faint field, a separate bug leaves an internal aperture value unset and crashes outright — confirmed by running the identical data through that EXOTIC build directly, with no TransitLab involved, reproducing the exact same crash. Since this could turn a run that previously completed with a real, if marginal, comparison star into a hard crash instead, require_comp_star is no longer set — leaving EXOTIC's own default ('y', require a real comp star) in place." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.8.0 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.8.0  —  2026-07-28" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #36): Rice/GZIP tile-compressed FITS (.fz) support. TransitLab now reads .fz files natively — no external decompression tool required. Image Analysis frame scanning, background estimation, PSF validation, dark frame loading, WCS-candidate search, and ASTAP plate solving all recognize .fz alongside .fits/.fit. The decoder handles RICE_1 and GZIP_1 tile compression with SUBTRACTIVE_DITHER_1/2 float unquantization (the scheme used by fpack/CFITSIO), and was validated pixel-by-pixel against astropy's own decompression of real observatory frames. HCOMPRESS_1 and PLIO_1 (used for large survey mosaics and pixel masks, not CCD/CMOS transit photometry frames) are not supported." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Multiple EXOTIC environments. The Setup tab now shows separate Stable and Pre-release/Development Build cards, each independently installable into its own isolated Python virtual environment. Previously installing a pre-release dev build required uninstalling the stable release first; now both can be installed at once, and a radio button on each card selects which environment runs on Save &amp; Run EXOTIC. A heads-up note appears when one environment is installed while the other is still using the older shared (non-isolated) install, so it's clear when both are fully separated." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #37): Import AAVSO Report (-pre) — File menu. Re-fits a previously-produced AAVSO Exoplanet Watch report (AAVSO_&lt;planet&gt;_&lt;date&gt;.txt) via EXOTIC's -pre mode, with no FITS files, comp star selection, or plate solve needed. The orbital solution (period, Rp/Rs, a/Rs, inclination, eccentricity, mid-transit time) is recovered exactly from the file's own embedded #PRIORS-XC/#RESULTS-XC metadata rather than a fresh NASA Exoplanet Archive query, so the result isn't affected by any NEA revisions made since the original run. Only stellar Teff/logg/FeH (needed solely for EXOTIC's limb-darkening calculation) come from a live NEA lookup. Output goes into a new pre_import_&lt;timestamp&gt; folder next to the source file — the original report is never overwritten." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Per-run output subfolders. Save &amp; Run now writes each run into its own subfolder of the Save Plots directory — '{Target Name}_{Obs Date}_Results{n}_{EXOTIC version}' (e.g. 'KELT-8 b_29-JUN-2026_Results1_4.3.1') — instead of overwriting the previous run's output files. {n} counts how many times that exact target + date has already been run, across any EXOTIC version, so re-processing the same night's data is always kept side by side. inits.json for that run is saved alongside its output." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: ASTAP 'Solve ALL images' status was misleading on datasets where many frames fail (e.g. MicroObservatory images). Individual frame failures no longer overwrite the live status with a scary-looking error for one file — the status now shows a running solved/failed count while scanning, and the final result is color-coded: green when every frame solved, yellow with a warning triangle when some frames failed but the scan is still usable (EXOTIC only needs one solved reference frame), and red only when zero frames solved. A related bug where the Parameters tab's plate-solve status always showed a green checkmark regardless of the actual outcome was also fixed." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix (issue #34): Results tab layout could overlap or hide the Submit Results panel (including the AAVSO login row) on a shorter window or when a large light-curve image was loaded. The log, prompt box, light-curve images, and Submit Results panel now share a single scrollable area, so nothing can be pushed off-screen or drawn over regardless of window size." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Save &amp; Run's pre-flight validation only checked that fields like RA, Dec, Orbital Period, and Mid-Transit Time were non-blank, not that they were valid numbers. A non-blank but unparseable value (e.g. a typo, stray character, or locale decimal mismatch) previously passed validation, then silently became a JSON null in inits.json, surfacing only much later as a confusing 'Warning: X is None' deep inside EXOTIC's own run. Save &amp; Run now checks that these fields actually parse as numbers and blocks the run up front with a message naming the exact field and invalid value. Number parsing also now always uses invariant culture, fixing a related case where a normal period-decimal value could silently fail to parse (or parse to the wrong value) on a non-US-English Windows locale." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the detected EXOTIC version used for Results-folder naming and for the 'Add Comparison Stars from AAVSO?' setting could go stale after switching between the Stable and Pre-release environments mid-session — it was only probed once per session and then cached regardless of which environment was actually active for a given run. It's now re-resolved from the currently active environment before every run." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: 'Stone + VSP' comp star method renamed to 'VSP + Stone' to match its actual priority order — VSP stars have always filled first, so 'Stone' listed first was backwards. Also fixed a related gap: if a selected VSP star failed PSF validation, the backfill replacement search didn't check candidate source at all, so a rejected VSP slot could end up refilled by a Stone candidate purely by list-order coincidence instead of by design. Backfill now explicitly tries another VSP candidate first, so VSP stars stay ahead of Stone stars even after PSF-driven replacement. An older saved 'Stone + VSP' preference is automatically remapped to the new name." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Stone / VSP + Stone comp star fetches could fail outright with 'No candidates found — Gaia: ...400...; VSP: ...400 (Bad Request)' on a non-US-English Windows locale (e.g. Bulgarian, Russian, German, French — any locale using a comma as the decimal separator). The Gaia DR3, APASS, and AAVSO VSP/VSX query URLs formatted RA/Dec/radius/magnitude values using the OS's current locale instead of a fixed format, so on an affected system the request embedded a comma (e.g. '283,306316') instead of a decimal point, which every one of those servers rejected as a malformed query. All affected query construction now forces an invariant (period-decimal) format regardless of locale. Also added session-log entries for the Fetch Comps click and its final result, which were previously silent — this specific failure never appeared in the diagnostics log even though it was visible on screen." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: numeric fields (RA, Dec, orbital period, Rp/Rs, a/Rs, inclination, pixel scale, filter wavelength, and more) could be silently inflated by orders of magnitude on locales that use a comma as the decimal separator (e.g. Spanish, Portuguese, German, French, Russian). Every numeric parse in TransitLab used a parsing style that permits thousands-group separators, so a value typed with a decimal comma that happened to match a valid 3-digit grouping — e.g. '12,345' meaning 12.345 — parsed successfully as 12345 instead of failing, with no error anywhere, surfacing only later as a geometry/fitting crash deep inside EXOTIC. All numeric parsing now goes through a shared parser that determines the decimal mark from the input's own shape (whichever of ',' or '.' appears last is the decimal point; any earlier one is discarded as a grouping character) rather than trusting the OS locale, so both '12,345' and '12.345' now parse to the correct value; input that still can't be resolved now fails validation loudly instead of silently producing a wrong number." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: after upgrading to v2.8.0, a pre-existing dev/pre-release EXOTIC build could be shown under the 'Stable' card instead of 'Pre-release'. The one-time migration that carries a pre-2.8.0 single-Python install into the new multi-environment Setup tab always labeled it 'Stable' without checking what was actually installed there. Check System now detects a migrated entry whose reported version is a dev/pre-release build and automatically moves it to the Pre-release card instead, logging why." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the Setup tab could show a green checkmark and 'Installed' for an environment whose EXOTIC install actually failed (e.g. a network outage partway through). Creating a new isolated environment registers its Python interpreter before the EXOTIC package install itself runs, and the installed indicator was keyed only to that interpreter existing — so an install that failed after the empty environment was created (git/pip unable to reach GitHub or PyPI) still displayed as successfully installed. The indicator now requires EXOTIC's own install step (or a fresh Check System scan) to positively confirm the package is actually present, not merely that the environment exists." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.7.1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.7.1  —  2026-07-18" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Download Full ldtk Library (Tools menu). Crawls the HTTPS PHOENIX mirrors used by EXOTIC's limb-darkening fallback, shows the total download size for confirmation, then downloads and installs the entire ldtk cache directly into ~/.ldtk — no manual extraction needed." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Automatic HTTPS fallback for ldtk network failures. If EXOTIC's FTP connection to the PHOENIX server times out (a known failure mode on some networks and when using EXOTIC 4.3.1, which has no fallback of its own), TransitLab detects the failure, fetches just the limb-darkening files needed for the current target over HTTPS, and automatically retries the run." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #29): NextAstro plate-solve option (Tools → Plate Solve Setup) — a third solver alongside Astrometry.net and ASTAP, using NextAstronomy's own hosted astrometry service. Sends only locally-detected star positions rather than the full FITS image, using RA/Dec and pixel scale as hints. Experimental — requires the EXOTIC 4.3.2 pre-release dev build, not yet part of any official EXOTIC release." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #35): Name column in Comp Star Details. Each selected comparison star now shows an identifying name — its AAVSO VSX designation if its position matches a known VSX entry, otherwise its full Gaia DR3 source ID — making it easier to look the star up in Simbad or Aladin." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: NextAstro plate-solve option can no longer be selected on a stable EXOTIC install. Plate Solve Setup now checks the installed EXOTIC version each time it opens and greys out NextAstro with an explanatory note unless the required pre-release dev build is detected (reported as '4.3.2.dev…', not a plain '4.3.2'). Previously selecting it without the pre-release build produced a plate-solve failure instead of being caught up front." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the 'Password Not Encrypted' warning and several User Guide / Tip of the Day mentions of the config/log folder location incorrectly said 'AppData\TransitLab' unconditionally, even on Mac and Linux — where TransitLab actually stores config.json, history.json, and session logs in ~/.config/TransitLab/, not anywhere called AppData. The password warning now shows the real resolved folder path directly; User Guide and Tip text now describe both locations." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #32): Stellar Variability Only checkbox (Parameters tab, top of Planet Parameters). Runs EXOTIC's stellar-variability-only reduction instead of fitting a transit model — useful for monitoring runs where no transit is expected. Written to inits.json's optional_info as 'stellar_variability_only'. Requires the EXOTIC 4.3.2 pre-release dev build, build 80 or later." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the AAVSO VSP comp star method could report a comparison star that has no actual photometry in your observation filter. The AAVSO VSP chart query ignored the filter band entirely, so a star with, say, only V-band data could be returned and used even when observing in SR — silently miscalibrating the result. The query now checks each candidate's published bands and only accepts stars with a real magnitude in the requested filter's VSP band, matching how the Stone comp method's own internal VSP query already worked." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Stellar Variability Only warning popup. Checking the box now shows a warning that this mode skips transit fitting entirely and should only be used on data that does not contain a transit, with a 'Don't show this warning again' option." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Stellar Variability Only mode showed the same light curve plot twice in the Results tab. EXOTIC saves an identical copy of the plot as both the main light curve image and a separate stellar-variability image when this mode is active; TransitLab now only displays it once. Normal transit-fit runs are unaffected — those two images are genuinely different plots in that mode." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the Darks / Flats / Biases / Save Plots directory pickers on the Data tab, and the Save Session Log dialog, no longer share a default folder. Neither ever set a starting location, so both silently fell back to the operating system's own generic 'last used folder' memory. Darks, Flats, Biases, and Save Plots now default to the Lights directory when they don't already have one of their own; the session log save dialog now tracks its own independent last-used folder." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: First-launch notice for v2.7.1. On the first run after upgrading, a one-time popup summarizes the new features added in this version, with a pointer to Revision History for full details." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.7.0 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.7.0  —  2026-06-23" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #13): Stone Comp Star Method. The comparison star pipeline, named after Geoffrey Stone (author of CompStarSelector), queries Gaia DR3, APASS DR9, and Gaia GSPC synthetic photometry to find and rank the best comp stars for each target. Magnitude source priority: GSPC (~0.01 mag) → APASS DR9 (~0.03 mag) → Gaia G→V polynomial → VSP. Three methods are available: 'AAVSO VSP' (AAVSO sequence only, no PSF validation), 'Stone + VSP' (full pipeline with VSP priority fill — recommended), and 'Stone' (full pipeline without VSP)." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: PSF Validation in Stone methods. After selecting comp candidates, the Stone pipeline measures each star's PSF directly from the FITS image. Stars that are saturated, have low SNR (&lt; 75), an elongated PSF, or an outlier FWHM are rejected and replaced from a ranked backfill pool. Up to 3 validation passes are run." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Comp Star Details popup. After a Stone or Stone + VSP fetch, a '⊞ Comp Details' button appears showing a per-star table with magnitude, uncertainty, source (GSPC/APASS/G→V/VSP), FWHM, SNR, angular separation, catalog origin, and PSF validation result for every selected comparison star." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Target Star RA was incorrectly converted from decimal degrees to decimal hours before being written to inits.json. EXOTIC expects decimal degrees. Observations processed with earlier versions should be re-run to produce a correctly-formed inits.json." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: EXOTIC's 'Thinking…' spinner animation now displays correctly in the Results log. Previously, carriage-return-delimited spinner frames accumulated in the buffer and were dumped as a block of text when the next newline arrived. Each frame now updates the log line in place." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix (issue #30): History tab now correctly populates all fields after a reduction with EXOTIC 4.3.2 or later. EXOTIC 4.3.2 renamed several keys in FinalParams_*.json (depth, Rp/Rs, and scatter fields). TransitLab now reads both old and new key names, ensuring full compatibility with EXOTIC 4.3.1 and 4.3.2+." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: EXOTIC 4.3.2 reduction runs no longer crash with a JSON decode error when AAVSO VSP is unavailable. EXOTIC 4.3.2 queries AAVSO VSP for comparison stars even when coordinates are already provided; if AAVSO returns an empty response, EXOTIC crashes. TransitLab now instructs EXOTIC to skip the VSP query when comparison star pixel coordinates are already selected." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: When EXOTIC exits with an error, the Results tab now displays the path to EXOTIC's exotic.log file so the detailed traceback is immediately accessible." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Import FinalParams JSON now correctly imports results from EXOTIC 4.3.2. The import handles both the 'FINAL PLANETARY PARAMETERS' wrapper structure (4.3.2+) and root-level structure (4.3.1), reads renamed depth and scatter keys, reads Rp/Rs from the new direct key, and extracts the planet name from the filename. Fully backward compatible with EXOTIC 4.3.1." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: History tab entries are now editable inline. Double-click any cell to edit; press Enter or Tab to confirm, Escape to cancel. Changes are saved automatically." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Exclusion counter in the Image Analysis tab no longer shows a stale count from the previous target after scanning a new FITS directory." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Stellar Variability plot is now correctly produced when running EXOTIC 4.3.1 with comparison stars pre-selected. TransitLab now probes the installed EXOTIC version before writing reduction parameters and only suppresses the AAVSO VSP comparison-star query (required to avoid a crash in EXOTIC 4.3.2) when EXOTIC 4.3.2 or later is detected. EXOTIC 4.3.1 users continue to receive the VSP query so vsp_comp_stars is populated and Stellar_Variability.png is generated." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix (issue #21): macOS update checker now correctly detects available releases. The asset lookup was filtering for .zip files only; macOS releases from v2.6.3 onwards use .dmg, so updates and previous versions were invisible on macOS. Both .zip and .dmg are now recognised." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: AAVSO Upload button now activates reliably after an EXOTIC run. A file-system caching issue could cause File.Exists() to return false for the report file a few minutes after scanning, even though the file was present. The button now uses a verification flag set at scan time instead of a live file-existence check." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Comp star query progress. While fetching comparison stars (Stone or Stone + VSP), the status line now shows live stage labels as the pipeline advances: querying Gaia DR3, querying VSP + APASS, calibrating magnitudes (GSPC), validating comp candidates (PSF). Mirror failover is also reported if a Gaia TAP endpoint times out. A 4 px animated progress bar appears below the status during the fetch and disappears when complete." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Removed (issue #8): Import NINA Star List removed from the Parameters tab Star Selection section." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #19): Acknowledgements — Michael Fitzgerald (NextAstronomy, Melbourne, Australia) added to Help → About for code contributions." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #16): custom TransitLab app icon, replacing the default Avalonia icon used since the app's first release." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #17): GitHub repository link added to Help → About." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #23): Save Password warning. When 'Save Password' is checked on the Results tab, a popup explains that the AAVSO password is stored as plain text in config.json inside the AppData\TransitLab folder and is not encrypted. Unchecking the box removes it from disk immediately." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #27): EXOTIC version shown in the Results tab. The installed EXOTIC version (e.g. 'EXOTIC 1.4.1') is displayed in the header row above the log window. It is populated asynchronously at startup and updated after each run — no manual check required." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #26): VSP chart North/East orientation controls. Two dropdowns ('N' and 'E') added to the Image Analysis VSP controls row. 'N' selects North direction on the chart (up / down); 'E' selects East direction (left / right). Defaults are North up, East left — the standard astronomical convention. The selected orientation is passed directly to the AAVSO VSP API." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: VSP Star field in Image Analysis now updates immediately when a new target is loaded. Previously the field retained the previous target's name until the session after next — it was only written when empty, so once any star name was set it was never replaced." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Stone Method verbose log. The Stone and Stone + VSP comparison star pipelines now stream a detailed step-by-step report into the Results tab log as they run. The 8-stage report covers: Gaia DR3 field query (star count, target G mag and BP-RP, candidate quality filtering), AAVSO VSP query (star count and Gaia enrichment), APASS DR9 query, frame projection and isolation (per-stage counts), scoring (top-10 table with score, Δmag, BP-RP, RUWE, and separation), GSPC synthetic photometry (match count and magnitude source breakdown), PSF validation (per-star FWHM/SNR/verdict for each pass, backfill events), and target PSF measurement with photon-limited precision estimate. The full report is also written to the session log." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Image Quality panel in Star Selection. After a Stone or Stone + VSP comp star query, a compact panel appears below the comp status bar showing four quality indicators: FWHM (mean across comp stars with uniformity label: uniform / mild / significant), Color match (active when the target's Gaia BP-RP index was found — enables the 30% color-similarity score component), Precision (photon-limited photometric precision in mmag estimated from the target's PSF SNR), and PSF grade (good / acceptable / marginal / poor). The panel is color-coded by grade and disappears when a new query starts." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Python version check now correctly enforces Python 3.10 as the minimum required version. Previously TransitLab accepted Python 3.8 and 3.9 as compatible; those versions cannot run EXOTIC 4.3.1 (which requires Python 3.10+). Users with Python 3.9 or below are now flagged and directed to install Python 3.10.11. Python 3.11 and 3.12 are also now recognised as supported rather than flagged as out of range." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: MObs Fetch List now correctly returns up to 30 days of observations. The previous URL fetched the default 10-day page from the MicroObservatory image directory, so setting Lookback Days to anything greater than 10 was silently ineffective. The URL now includes SortRange=30 to request the full 30-day archive from the server. The client-side lookback filter continues to restrict results to the user-configured number of days." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: ASTAP plate solver now uses a computed field-of-view (FOV) instead of -fov 0. The hardcoded -fov 0 flag instructed ASTAP to iterate every FOV value from 9.5° down to 0.8° on each frame. On small-format images (e.g. MicroObservatory 512×512), this produced spurious solutions with as few as 3 matching quads and a completely wrong CD matrix — wrong pixel scale and orientation — which prevented EXOTIC from using PSF photometry and caused residual scatter of 55–58%. TransitLab now computes FOV = NAXIS2 × pixel scale / 3600 and passes the precise value to ASTAP. The pixel scale is taken from the Pixel Scale field on the Parameters tab." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: ASTAP plate solver now rejects solutions with fewer than 4 matching quads. ASTAP requires a minimum of 3 quads to declare a solution, but a 3-quad match is statistically unreliable and can return a CD matrix with a completely wrong scale. TransitLab now parses the quad count from ASTAP output and fails the solve if fewer than 4 quads matched, triggering a re-solve attempt or a clear error message." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: ASTAP catalog directory flag corrected from -wcs to -d. When a separate catalog directory was configured in Plate Solve Setup, TransitLab was passing -wcs &lt;path&gt; to ASTAP. -wcs (no argument) writes a .wcs output file; it is not the catalog directory flag. The correct flag is -d &lt;path&gt;. This only affected users who configured a custom catalog directory separate from the ASTAP executable directory." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Comp Star Details popup column alignment corrected. The [?] help button was placed inside the header row, making the header Grid narrower than the data row Grids and misaligning all columns from Source onward. The [?] button has been moved to the footer bar (left of Close), and column widths have been adjusted so every column header aligns with its data." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Comp Star Details PSF status label for unmeasured stars changed from '⚠ PSF' to 'N/M' (not measured). Stars added from the backfill pool after all three PSF validation passes are complete are never measured — FWHM and SNR remain blank and the status correctly reads N/M rather than implying a PSF check failure." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Shift+Click range exclusion in Image Analysis. Click the first frame in the list, hold Shift and click the last frame to highlight the range, then click any Excl checkbox in the selection — all highlighted rows are toggled together. Single-row behavior is unchanged." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: Stone comp star selection now uses tiered RUWE quality gates. Instead of a fixed RUWE &lt; 1.4 threshold, the pipeline tries RUWE &lt; 1.1 first; if fewer than 8 candidates survive all other filters, it relaxes to RUWE &lt; 1.2, then to RUWE &lt; 1.4 on very sparse fields. This applies the strictest available astrometric quality cut without starving sparse fields of candidates. The active threshold is reported in the Stone pipeline log (Results tab)." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: Stone comp star selection now requires Gaia flux-over-error (FOE) &gt; 200, raised from the previous threshold of &gt; 100. Stars with FOE 100–200 have non-trivial Gaia photometric uncertainty and are marginal candidates for differential photometry. Raising the floor tightens the pool quality, particularly on crowded fields where fainter and noisier candidates are more common." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: Stone PSF validation SNR floor raised from &lt; 50 to &lt; 75. During PSF validation, comp star candidates with a measured SNR below 75 are now rejected and replaced from the backfill pool. The previous threshold of 50 allowed marginally noisy stars into the ensemble; raising it ensures only well-detected stars contribute to the light curve." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Stone comp star selection now cross-checks candidates against the AAVSO Variable Star Index (VSX). After the Gaia candidate pool is built, the pipeline queries VSX for all known variables in the field and hard-excludes any candidate within 5 arcseconds of a match. VSX is complementary to Gaia's internal variability flag — a star can appear in VSX without being flagged in Gaia DR3 (Barlad V46 in the TOI-1259 A field is an example). If the VSX query fails, the check is skipped and the pipeline continues normally. Excluded stars and their VSX names are reported in the Stone pipeline log." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Configurable comp star limit. The maximum number of comparison stars selected by all comp methods can now be set from 1 to 25 (default 10) via Tools → Settings → Comp Stars. The active limit is shown in the pipeline log header. Raising the limit above 10 is recommended only after tightening the quality gates (RUWE, FOE, SNR floor) so that additional candidates are genuinely better than the current ensemble average." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: 'Stone Method' settings renamed to 'Comp Stars'. The maximum comparison star limit applies to all comp methods (AAVSO VSP, Stone + VSP, and Stone), not just the Stone pipeline. Menu item, dialog title, tooltip, and User Guide references updated accordingly." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: Comparison star fetch is now manual. After the plate solve completes, a 'Fetch Comps' button becomes active in the Star Selection section. Click it to run the selected method. A 'Cancel' button is visible while the fetch is in progress. This decouples method selection from the Read FITS Header action — the user can choose or change the comp method at any time before clicking Fetch Comps, rather than having to pre-select it before the header is read. The selected method is saved and restored between sessions." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Per-method description text. A description line beneath the Comp Method dropdown updates dynamically as you select each option: AAVSO VSP describes the VSP-only workflow; Stone + VSP summarises the full scored pipeline with VSP priority fill (recommended); Stone describes the catalog-only pipeline without VSP." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Auto pixel-scale correction from Astrometry.net WCS. After a successful Astrometry.net plate solve, if the pixel scale derived from the WCS CD matrix differs from the configured Pixel Scale by more than 5%, TransitLab automatically updates the Pixel Scale field for the session. This prevents ASTAP from receiving an incorrect FOV hint on subsequent solves — a wrong scale was the root cause of ASTAP quad-matching failures on telescopes whose saved pixel scale did not match the actual image scale. The status bar identifies the old and new values; open Tools → Settings → Solvers and click Save to persist the corrected scale across sessions." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: ASTAP small-image warning. When ASTAP emits 'Warning, small image dimensions!!' — indicating the image is too small for reliable quad centroiding — TransitLab now captures this and replaces the generic 'No solution found' message with an actionable explanation: 'image too small for ASTAP quad-matching at X.XX&quot;/px — switch to Astrometry.net'. This is the expected result for MicroObservatory (MObs) frames (650×500 at 5&quot;/px): star centroids span less than one pixel at this scale, so ASTAP's geometric quad matching cannot converge. Astrometry.net succeeds on the same frames. When all frames fail due to this condition, the status bar shows a single summary: 'ASTAP: image dimensions too small for quad-matching — 0/N solved. Switch to Astrometry.net.'" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: ASTAP no longer re-solves all frames unnecessarily when the first file in the FITS directory is a bad or dark frame. Previously, if the first non-excluded FITS file had no plate solution (common when a dark or saturated frame appears first alphabetically), TransitLab re-ran ASTAP across all frames on every Read FITS Header click, even though a valid WCS was already present in every other frame. TransitLab now scans up to 5 additional files in the directory when the first file has no CTYPE1; if any already carries a WCS, the plate solve is skipped and that file's WCS is used directly. A log entry '[FITS] WCS found in &lt;filename&gt; — skipping plate solve' records when this shortcut is taken." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Comparison star fetch no longer fails with 'No plate solution' when ASTAP Solve ALL images produces a partial solve. Previously, after an all-frames ASTAP run, the path passed to the comparison star services was always the first file in the directory — which may be a dark or saturated frame that ASTAP can never solve. Both AavsoCompService and GaiaCompService read WCS directly from the FITS file to convert catalog coordinates to pixel positions, so a path to an unsolved file always returned 'No plate solution'. TransitLab now tracks the first file that ASTAP actually solved and uses that path for all subsequent WCS operations." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Clear ldtk Cache. Added a 'Clear ldtk Cache' item under Tools that deletes EXOTIC's ldtk limb-darkening model cache (~/.ldtk). Safe to run — ldtk automatically re-downloads any needed files on the next run. Useful when a reduction fails with an 'Empty or corrupt FITS file' error caused by an interrupted download." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Automatic detection of a corrupted ldtk cache during an EXOTIC run. If EXOTIC's output reports 'Empty or corrupt FITS file' — an ldtk limb-darkening cache issue unrelated to the user's own FITS data — TransitLab now shows a dialog explaining the cause and pointing to Tools → Clear ldtk Cache, instead of leaving the user with a raw Python traceback." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Pre-release branch URLs are remembered. The EXOTIC Setup 'Pre-release / Development Build' field is now an editable dropdown; any URL installed from is automatically remembered for future sessions, with a Remove button to prune old entries." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Warning when VSP comp stars fail PSF validation. When 'Stone + VSP' finds AAVSO VSP candidates but none survive the PSF/SNR quality filter, the comp status line and pipeline log now explicitly report how many VSP stars were found and that zero survived, rather than silently reporting a Gaia-only result indistinguishable from plain 'Stone'." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Comparison star pixel coordinates no longer carry over from the previous target. Clicking 'Read FITS Header' now also clears the Comparison Stars X,Y field and any cached comp star details, matching the existing Target Star X,Y reset. Previously only the target coordinates were cleared, which could cause stale comp star positions to be reused on a new target." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Comp star status text now wraps correctly. The green status line summarizing the selected comparison stars was clipped at the window edge instead of wrapping to a new line, particularly with longer messages such as the new VSP quality-filter warning." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: Default comp star method changed to 'AAVSO VSP' (was 'Stone + VSP') for new installations." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: [?] help popups are now scrollable. Previously the popup window grew to fit its full text unconditionally, which could push it off-screen with no way to reach the rest of the content or the OK button. Long popups now show a scrollbar with the OK button always pinned and reachable." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Quick Start and User Guide star-selection instructions updated for the new manual comp star workflow. Previous text described AAVSO comps fetching automatically and referenced the removed 'Import NINA Star List' feature; both have been corrected to describe selecting a comp method and clicking Fetch Comps." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: First-launch notice for v2.7.0. On the first run after upgrading, a one-time popup summarizes the new Comp Star Selection methods and the new manual Fetch Comps step, with a pointer to the User Guide for full details." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.6.5 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.6.5  —  2026-05-20" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Submit Feedback — updated authentication token; the feature is now working again." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Settings — when 'Save Password' is checked for AAVSO credentials, a notice is shown that the password is stored as plain text in config.json. The password is also deleted from config.json immediately when 'Save Password' is unchecked, rather than waiting until the next app exit." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.6.4 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.6.4  —  2026-05-15" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: AAVSO Upload button is now available on app launch if a report file from the previous session exists. The Save Plots directory is scanned at startup so the Upload button activates without needing to re-run EXOTIC." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix (issue #3): Automation no longer freezes on blocking dialogs. All validation dialogs in Save &amp; Run (FITS header read required, missing fields, suspicious Rp/Rs) and the EXOTIC runtime resolver are suppressed during an automation run — the sequence logs the reason and aborts cleanly instead." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Automation no longer blocks on the 'Maximum Comp Stars' dialog when 10 comparison stars are already selected from a previous session. The existing comp stars are cleared automatically so a fresh auto-selection can proceed." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Running back-to-back automation sequences for different targets no longer produces wildly out-of-bounds target pixel coordinates. The previous plate solve (WCS) and RA/Dec coordinates are now cleared before the new target's FITS header is read, ensuring the auto-select step uses only the fresh plate solution and the correct target coordinates from NEA." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: Automation redesigned. The 'Monitor window' folder-polling model (which watched for file count stability over 30 seconds) has been removed. Automation now simply waits for the configured start time and launches the sequence immediately — no folder polling." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Automation Armed banner. When automation is armed, a slowly flashing green '⬤ AUTOMATION ARMED' banner appears above the tab strip. A MM:SS countdown to the start time is shown alongside it; once the sequence starts the banner reads 'Running…' and disappears when done." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change (issue #5): Image Analysis — 'Auto-exclude Flagged' button renamed to 'Exclude Flagged' and repositioned to sit alongside 'Restore Excluded', making the pair of actions visually symmetric." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Clicking 'Restore Excluded' no longer overwrites the scan file count shown in the status area. The scan count is now only updated by the scan itself." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: A stale exotic.log file left in the output folder from a previous run no longer causes a flood of PermissionError: [WinError 32] log rotation errors in the diagnostics log. TransitLab now deletes exotic.log from the working directory before each EXOTIC launch so the log rotation handler always starts fresh." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Diagnostics log now records user actions. Operationally significant button clicks (Scan Frames, Read FITS Header, Exclude Flagged, Restore Excluded, Auto Select Target, Auto Select Comps, Save inits Only, Load inits, Clear All Fields, Cancel EXOTIC, Check for Updates, Download Update, Skip Update, Browse buttons for all directory fields) are written to the session log as they occur. Key field values (target name, obs date, filter, pixel scale, camera type, binning, obs codes, directory paths, and more) are logged automatically once the user finishes entering them." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #10): Parameters tab — [?] help buttons added next to each section header (Equipment, Observer Information, Observatory / Location, Plate Solve, Star Selection, Planet Parameters). Clicking [?] opens a concise popup explaining the purpose of each field in that section." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Results tab — [?] help buttons added next to the EXOTIC Log and Submit Results section headers. Clicking [?] explains the Auto prompts toggle, Pause Log button, how to save a log copy via Diagnostics, AAVSO login, Site and Equipment Package selection, and the AAVSO Variability (WebObs) button functions." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Image Analysis tab — [?] help button added to the left of the Scan Files button. Clicking [?] explains every function in the tab: frame scanning, sigma flagging, exclude/restore, dark subtract, the VSP chart controls, image viewer controls, and the Pick Target Star / Pick Comp Stars workflow." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Data tab — [?] help buttons added next to the Directories and MicroObservatory (MObs) section headers. Clicking [?] explains the purpose of each directory field and every MObs control (lookback days, Fetch List, Download Selected, Use This Data, and the default download directory option)." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: MObs Telescope selector removed. Telescope is now fixed to Cecilia. User Guide and help text updated accordingly." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Visualizer tab — [?] help button added to the left of the Play button. Clicking [?] explains every control: Play/Pause, Reset, Speed, Orbit scrub, Parameters popup, Load Photometry, the transit geometry and light curve panels, and all derived quantities shown at the bottom." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: History tab — [?] help button added to the left of the Export CSV button. Clicking [?] explains the Export CSV/XLSX, Delete Selected, Import FinalParams JSON, and Import CSV/XLSX buttons, and describes every column in the history table." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #12): Tip of the Day. A popup appears at startup showing one of 47 tips covering every area of TransitLab — directory setup, image analysis, plate solving, NEA parameters, AAVSO submission, the Visualizer, automation, and more. Use Prev/Next to browse. Uncheck 'Show tips at startup' in the popup or in Tools → Notifications to disable. Tips cycle in order and resume where you left off on the next launch." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #15): Diagnostics — Load Previous Log button. Opens a file picker starting directly in %AppData%\TransitLab\logs\ so any previous session log can be reviewed and saved without navigating to AppData manually." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #14): Help → Previous Versions. Lists all GitHub releases with version number, release date, and platform availability. Select any release and click Download to save the ZIP to a folder of your choice." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement (issue #18): MObs — Lookback Days value is now remembered between sessions. The number of days entered in the Lookback Days field is saved to config.json and restored on next launch." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New (issue #4): Visualizer — Starspot Effect. The Visualizer Parameters sandbox adds a Starspot Effect section. Enable a configurable dark spot (radius, temperature contrast ΔT, X/Y position) and observe the resulting effects on the model light curve: an unocculted spot depresses the out-of-transit baseline (Zellem et al. 2017, ApJ 844, 1); a spot on the transit chord produces a characteristic in-transit flux bump when the planet occults it (Silva 2003, A&amp;A 400, 723). Physical models are cited in Help → About TransitLab → Acknowledgements." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.6.3 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.6.3  —  2026-04-25" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Linux initial release." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Python version warning dialog. If Check System detects a Python version outside the supported range (3.8–3.10), a warning dialog is shown advising that EXOTIC officially supports Python 3.8–3.10 and that Python 3.10.11 is recommended." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: On Linux, the Download &amp; Install Python button is hidden. Python must be installed manually on Linux before using the Setup wizard. All other setup functions (Install EXOTIC, Uninstall EXOTIC) work normally once Python is detected." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Automatic update checker. TransitLab checks for a new release on GitHub each time it starts. If an update is available, a banner appears at the top of the window showing the new version number with Download and Skip options. Download prompts for a save folder (defaulting to Downloads) and shows progress. Help → Check for Updates allows a manual check at any time." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Submit Feedback. Help → Submit Feedback opens a form to submit a bug report or feature request directly to the TransitLab GitHub repository. The type, summary, description, optional contact email, and auto-detected version and OS are included. Reports are publicly visible on GitHub." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.6.2 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.6.2  —  2026-04-24" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: macOS initial release. No functional changes to the Windows version." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: The 'Download &amp; Install Python' button in Python &amp; EXOTIC Setup now relabels itself to 'Reinstall Python' when Python is already detected, making it clear the button can be used to repair a corrupt Python installation. The button is always enabled after Check System runs." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.6.1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.6.1  —  2026-04-23" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Internal: project renamed from ExoticLauncher to TransitLab throughout — namespaces, assembly name, and all source file references. No functional changes." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Operation status alerts. TransitLab now plays a short Windows Device Connect sound on success or Device Disconnect sound on failure after each NEA target fetch, plate solve, and AAVSO comparison star fetch. Controlled by the Operation status alerts toggle in Tools → Settings → Notifications. Enabled by default." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: NEA fetch failure and AAVSO fetch timeout no longer leave the AAVSO Comps status permanently stuck at 'Fetching…'. When the NEA fetch fails, the AAVSO comp fetch now resumes using WCS image-centre coordinates rather than waiting forever. When the AAVSO HTTP request times out, the timeout is now treated as a retriable failure rather than being silently swallowed." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: EXOTIC Setup install buttons (Install EXOTIC, Install Pre-release, Install Python) caused the entire application to close immediately when clicked. A recursive call in the internal Report helper introduced in v2.5.6 caused an unrecoverable StackOverflowException on every install operation." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Uninstall EXOTIC button added to the Python &amp; EXOTIC Setup wizard. Removes EXOTIC only (pip uninstall exotic -y); Python is left intact. Enabled after Check System confirms EXOTIC is present. To reinstall after uninstalling, click Install EXOTIC." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: 'EXOTIC Setup' renamed to 'Python &amp; EXOTIC Setup' in the Tools menu and throughout the User Guide." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: 'Install / Upgrade EXOTIC' button renamed to 'Install EXOTIC'." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: Dark Subtract checkbox in Image Analysis tab now defaults to unchecked." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: Visualizer sunspots are now smaller (0.5–2% of star radius) and more numerous (8–15 per star), closer to the appearance of real white-light solar images." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.6.0 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.6.0  —  2026-04-23" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Automation feature accessible via Tools → Settings → Automation (Settings is now a submenu; Notifications and Automation each open their own window). Configure a monitor folder, an optional wall-clock start time, and a monitoring window. When armed, TransitLab polls the folder every 10 seconds and displays a live MM:SS countdown. Once the FITS file count has been stable for 30 consecutive seconds, the full reduction pipeline fires automatically." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Automation sequence: properly waits for each async operation to complete before proceeding — plate solve and NEA fetch are both awaited (up to 5 minutes) before auto-selecting the target star; AAVSO comp fetch completion is confirmed before auto-selecting comparison stars. All confirmation dialogs (e.g. Excluded Frames) are automatically accepted during an automation run. The sequence aborts with a clear log message if no frames survive auto-exclusion, or if the plate solve / NEA times out." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: automation scan could silently find 0 frames on the second (and subsequent) runs. Disabling dark subtract at sequence start fired a fire-and-forget re-scan (HandleDarkSubtractToggledAsync) when frames from the previous run were still loaded. That scan set IsScanRunning=true, so the explicit scan 200 ms later saw CanExecute=false and returned immediately with an empty frame list, aborting the sequence. Fixed by polling IsScanRunning=false after the dark-subtract clear before issuing the explicit scan, and again after the scan command returns (to let the Dispatcher.Post that populates Frames flush on the UI thread)." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: AAVSO comparison star fetch now retries automatically once if the first attempt returns no results. The status area shows the failure reason and a 10-second countdown before the retry, so the user is informed throughout. If the retry also fails, the final error is displayed as before. This handles transient network failures that previously required a manual Retry Comps click." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: User Guide restructured. Settings section (11) added with Notifications (11a) and Automation (11b) subsections. Diagnostics renumbered to section 12." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Operation status alerts. TransitLab now plays a short Windows Device Connect sound on success or Device Disconnect sound on failure after each NEA target fetch, plate solve, and AAVSO comparison star fetch. The alerts can be enabled or disabled via Tools → Settings → Notifications. Enabled by default." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.5.6 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.5.6  —  2026-04-23" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Session logging. A timestamped diagnostics log file (exotic_diagnostics_&lt;datetime&gt;.log) is written automatically to %AppData%\TransitLab\logs\ each time TransitLab runs. The five most recent sessions are kept and older files are deleted automatically." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Tools → Diagnostics window. Opens the current session log in a scrollable viewer with a Save Log button to export it as a .txt file. This replaces the per-area Save Log and Copy Log buttons that were previously scattered across tabs." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Removed: 'Copy Log' and 'Save Log' buttons from the Results tab (EXOTIC log). The session log written to %AppData%\TransitLab\logs\ contains all EXOTIC output and can be saved via Tools → Diagnostics." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Removed: 'Save Log…' button from the EXOTIC Setup tab. Setup activity is captured in the session log." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: comprehensive error and event logging throughout the app. Every operation that can silently fail now writes a tagged entry to the session log: [Config] / [History] file load/save errors; [FITS] read errors and missing-file warnings; [NEA] query results; [AavsoComp] fetch results and failures; [AAVSO Login] / [AAVSO Upload] outcome; [PlateSolve] and [PlateSolve/ASTAP] results (per-frame and all-frames summary); [Run] validation failures and the exact EXOTIC command launched; [History] import/export errors; [Setup] Python and EXOTIC install progress; [MObs] fetch and download results. The session log viewable in Tools → Diagnostics captures enough detail to diagnose virtually any problem a user could encounter." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: plate solve logging expanded. For Astrometry.net: the Python path and file name are logged at start, and all meaningful status lines streamed by the solver (Uploading, Waiting, submission ID, job result) now appear in the log in addition to the progress indicator. For ASTAP: every output line the solver produces — star count, solution RA/Dec/plate scale on success, or full error trace on failure — is now logged. Previously only a single line on failure reached the log." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: EXOTIC Setup install process fully logged. Every status message and all pip/winget output lines generated during Python installation, EXOTIC installation, Git installation, and repair operations are now captured in the diagnostics log alongside the Setup window's own output display. This allows remote diagnosis of install failures from the log file alone." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: Visualizer geometry panel refined. The outer glow ring (which extended past the star into surrounding panel areas at smaller window sizes) has been removed. Faculae (light-coloured blobs on the star surface) have been removed. Sunspot rendering improved — four offset penumbra lobes at different aspect ratios form an irregular organic outline, with a two-layer umbra (dark region and darker inner core), closer to the appearance of real solar active regions." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: Visualizer impact parameter b can now be set to negative values (orbital inclination past 90°), placing the transit chord below the stellar equator. The b slider range is extended to ±1.2 and the inclination slider to 60°–120°. Both are clamped so the chord cannot extend beyond the limb-darkening halo (b ≤ 1.18), preventing the planet path from escaping the visible star area." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: Visualizer sunspot pattern is now unique per target. Count (2–6), position, and size are randomised using the target name as a seed, so each planet displays a different arrangement that remains stable during animation. Sizes range from very small up to the previous fixed maximum." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.5.5 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.5.5  —  2026-04-21" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: ASTAP 'Solve ALL images' reported 'failed' whenever any single frame could not be solved (e.g. bad or excluded frames still in the directory). The solve now succeeds as long as at least one frame is solved successfully; individual frame failures are reported in the status but do not block the pipeline." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: clicking 'Save &amp; Run EXOTIC' switched to the Visualizer tab instead of the Results tab. Caused by a stale tab index (4 = Visualizer) in the EXOTIC launch routine left over from a previous tab-order change. Corrected to index 3 (Results)." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: EXOTIC Log text size increased by 50% (from 13 pt to 20 pt) for better readability. The prompt input area uses the same increased size." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: on 1920×1080 screens, the vertical divider on the Parameters tab was too close to the left, causing the Plate Solve 'Cancel' button to be clipped. The divider has been moved to a 5:3 column ratio (left panel wider, Planetary Parameters narrower), giving the equipment/solve/star section more room." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: the Visualizer 'Parameters ▶' popup opened off-screen to the right of the main window on 1920×1080 displays. It now opens centered over the main window. Users with larger screens can drag it to any position." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: after a plate solve triggered by 'Read FITS Header', the status next to the button remained at 'filename | Starting plate solve…' even after the solve completed. It now updates to show the same completion or failure message as the Plate Solve status on the Parameters tab." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: T₂/T₃ contact markers on the Visualizer were drawn almost on top of T₁/T₄ at high inclinations (impact parameter near 0), creating a confusing stacked pair of ticks at the stellar limb. T₂/T₃ are now suppressed when their pixel separation from T₁/T₄ is less than 20 px — they reappear automatically at lower inclinations once there is enough space to label them clearly." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: clicking 'Install / Upgrade EXOTIC' in EXOTIC Setup did not revert a GitHub branch (dev) build back to the stable PyPI release. pip treated the installed dev version (e.g. 4.3.2.dev22+…) as newer than any stable release and skipped the install. The install step now uses --force-reinstall so the latest stable release is always fetched from PyPI regardless of what is currently installed." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Completion sound is now configurable under Tools → Settings. Choose from three built-in Windows sounds (Tada, Chime, Ding), silence (None), or a custom audio file (WAV, MP3, AIFF) from your computer. A Test button lets you preview the selected sound before saving. The default sound is Tada." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.5.4 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.5.4  —  2026-04-20" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: MicroObservatory observations list (Data tab) was clipped to a fixed height of 220px, showing only ~6 rows regardless of how many results were fetched. Changed to a minimum height so the list grows to display all results, with the outer scroll area handling overflow." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: 'Submit Results' section on the Results tab (AAVSO login credentials, Upload buttons) could be partially clipped at certain window sizes, hiding the section header and login row. Fixed by restructuring the DockPanel layout so the Submit Results panel reserves its space before the log and light curve areas, ensuring it is always fully visible." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: 'Install Pre-release' button in EXOTIC Setup was incorrectly disabled until Check System had been run. The button is now enabled as soon as a branch URL is pasted." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: EXOTIC Setup now automatically installs Git for Windows if it is not found on the machine when installing a pre-release build. Git is required by pip to clone from GitHub. Installation is handled silently via winget (built into Windows 10/11) with no user action required beyond approving a UAC prompt if it appears." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.5.3 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.5.3  —  2026-04-19" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: 'Lights Directory' rename and 'Save Plots Directory' repositioning (both introduced in v2.5.2) were applied to the wrong source file and had no visible effect. Corrected — the Data tab now shows 'Lights Directory' at the top and 'Save Plots Directory' below Biases Directory." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: User data (config.json and history.json) is now stored in %AppData%\TransitLab\ instead of beside the executable. Settings and submission history are preserved automatically across upgrades and reinstalls. On first launch after upgrading, existing files are migrated from the old location automatically." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: EXOTIC Setup wizard now includes a Pre-release / Development Build section. Paste a GitHub branch URL (e.g. https://github.com/rzellem/EXOTIC.git@branch-name) and click Install Pre-release to install directly from that branch via pip. Use only when directed by the EXOTIC developers. To return to the stable release, click Install / Upgrade EXOTIC. Requires Git to be installed on the machine." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.5.2 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.5.2  —  2026-04-18" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Bug fix: T1/T4 contact tick marks in the Visualizer now correctly align with the star's limb rather than the planet's center. Ticks are shifted inward by Rp (T1/T4) or outward by Rp (T2/T3) so they mark the planet's edge position at the moment of contact — the standard astronomical convention." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Orbit scrub slider added to the Visualizer. Drag it to manually position the planet at any orbital phase (0–1). Works alongside the animation — dragging while playing will scrub to a new position and the animation resumes from there." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Star color now adapts to the host star's effective temperature (Teff). A/F stars (Teff &gt; 7500 K) appear white-blue; G-type (solar) yellow; K-type orange; M-type red-orange. Falls back to G-type if Teff is not entered." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Planet appearance adapts to estimated size class based on Rp/Rs. Gas giants (k ≥ 0.09) show Jupiter-style blue-grey atmospheric banding with a storm oval (when large enough). Neptune-class (k 0.05–0.09) show teal-blue banding. Small/rocky (k &lt; 0.05) appear grey-blue with subtle shading." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Visualizer geometry panel now shows the target/planet name at the top of the display, updated automatically when the planet name or host star name changes on the Parameters tab." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: 'IN TRANSIT / out of transit' status label removed from the Visualizer geometry panel. The target name now occupies that space at the top of the panel." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: Visualizer tab moved after the Results tab. New tab order: Data → Image Analysis → Parameters → Results → Visualizer → History." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: Light curve display window narrowed to ±1.5×T14 (total 3×T14) from the previous ±3.5×T14. The transit event now fills more of the chart area." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: sunspot penumbra shapes are now irregular — two offset, differently-proportioned ellipses overlap to form a non-circular outline, closer to the appearance of real solar active regions." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Settings dialog added under Tools → Settings. Currently offers a 'Play sound when results are ready' option that plays the Windows Tada sound when the EXOTIC light curve image appears in the Results tab." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: App footer copyright line updated to plain attribution (no copyright claim). About dialog updated to 'Free to use for personal and non-commercial use', adds Claude Code development credit, and adds AAVSO acknowledgement." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: Orbit scrub slider moved into the control bar next to the Speed slider. Slider range is now limited to the visible transit window (±1.5×T₁₄) so small movements don't overshoot the transit. Scrubbing while paused now correctly redraws the geometry panel." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Improvement: Light curve transit depth annotation relabelled from 'Δ = …%' to 'Transit depth …%' and moved from the top-right to the bottom-right of the plot area, where it sits adjacent to the feature it describes." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Visualizer split view is now 50/50 by default (was 40/60 geometry/light curve)." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Impact parameter b can now be adjusted directly in the Visualizer Parameters popup using a dedicated slider. Previously only Rp/Rs, a/Rs, inclination, and period were editable." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Visualizer parameters are now fully sandboxed — changes made in the Parameters popup update only the transit animation and do not write back to the Parameters tab. The original NEA values are preserved. A 'Reset to Parameters Tab Values' button restores all sliders to the imported values." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Time offset from mid-transit is shown in the lower-right corner of the geometry panel and updates in real time during animation and scrubbing (e.g. −1.23 h, +0.00 h)." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Stellar density ρ★/ρ☉ derived from transit geometry is shown in the derived quantities bar at the bottom of the Visualizer. Computed as ρ★/ρ☉ ≈ 0.01341 × (a/Rs)³ / P² and updates with sandbox parameters." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Load Photometry button at the bottom of the Visualizer lets users overlay observed relative flux data (CSV or TXT) on the model light curve as yellow scatter points. First column defaults to phase, second to flux; headers 'phase' and 'flux' are recognised automatically." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Light curve model upgraded from uniform-source to quadratic limb-darkening using numerical radial integration — I(μ) = 1 − u₁(1−μ) − u₂(1−μ)². Default coefficients u₁ = 0.40, u₂ = 0.30 (approximately solar). Both coefficients are adjustable via sliders in the Visualizer Parameters popup." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Time offset from mid-transit now displayed at the top of the red cursor line in the light curve panel (to the left of the flux readout), updating in real time during animation and scrubbing." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: Transit depth annotation moved from the bottom-right of the light curve plot to directly beneath the transit trough, centered at mid-transit (phase 0.5)." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Spectral type readout added to the derived quantities bar, to the right of Stellar Density. Displays the spectral class letter (O through M/L-T) and a brief description (e.g. 'G · yellow, solar-type') derived from the host star Teff." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Fix: Main window default size reduced to 1400×960 and minimum size reduced to 1280×760. Resolves an issue where the window could not fit on 1920×1080 displays running at 125% or higher Windows display scaling." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: Spectral type description for K-type stars corrected from 'orange dwarf' (informal/non-standard) to 'orange, cooler than Sun'." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: 'FITS Files Directory' label on the Data tab renamed to 'Lights Directory'." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Change: 'Save Plots Directory' moved to the bottom of the Directories section on the Data tab, below Biases Directory." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.5.1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.5.1  —  2026-04-17" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Bug fix: browsing to a new FITS directory now clears all session-specific fields (date, lat/lon/elevation, and all planet and star parameters). Previously those fields retained values from the previous session, which could silently submit stale planet data to EXOTIC." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Bug fix: EXOTIC log Freeze button renamed to '⏸ Pause Log' and converted to a toggle button. When active, auto-scroll is suspended so long log output can be reviewed while EXOTIC is still running. Clicking again resumes auto-scroll." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Bug fix: clicking 'Pick Target Star' or 'Pick Comp Stars' while a non-first image is displayed now shows a modal dialog explaining that picks must be made on the first non-excluded frame. Previously a silent yellow status message appeared that was easy to miss." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Bug fix: Table of Contents links in the User Guide now scroll to the correct heading position using direct scroll offset. Previously they used BringIntoView(), which could land on the wrong section." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Bug fix: Results tab description of the curve-fitting algorithm corrected — now accurately describes nested sampling (Ultranest/Dynesty) rather than the outdated MCMC description." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Bug fix: dark subtract is now enabled by default in the Image Analysis tab. The toggle was previously off by default." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Bug fix: image viewer now correctly applies dark subtraction to all display paths (render, histogram, cursor ADU readout). Previously the dark-subtracted pixel array was not used for display even when dark subtract was enabled." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Bug fix: AAVSO comp star fetch no longer attempts a WCS fallback while a NEA query is still running. The 'Waiting for NEA query' deferral now correctly fires before the WCS read, avoiding a race condition where an incomplete fetch could lock in WCS-derived coordinates rather than the more accurate planet parameters." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: all planetary parameter fields on the Parameters tab now show a 2-second hover tooltip describing the parameter, its units, and typical value ranges." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: ASTAP Plate Solve Setup now includes a 'Solve ALL images' checkbox. When checked, clicking Plate Solve runs ASTAP on every FITS file in the FITS directory, writing WCS to each frame. Default is off (solve first image only)." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Bug fix: image panning in the Image Analysis tab was broken. Pointer events were subscribed to the Image element, which is not reliably hit-testable in Avalonia. Fixed by routing all pointer interactions through a transparent parent Grid that covers the full image area." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Bug fix: Visualizer light curve was inverted — the transit dip rendered as a peak above 1.0 instead of a drop below it. Caused by a typo in the Mandel &amp; Agol (2002) partial-overlap formula: the fourth factor in Heron's triangle area was (z+k+1) instead of (z+k−1), inflating the overlap area and producing flux values greater than 1." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Visualizer geometry panel now annotates the stellar limb darkening glow rings with a labelled pointer line ('Limb darkening') at the upper-left of the star." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: all text labels in the Visualizer geometry panel enlarged by 50% (contact labels T₁–T₄, R★, Rp/R★, impact parameter b, transit status)." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New: Visualizer animation now auto-loops. When the planet exits the display window at egress, the animation holds at that position for 1.5 seconds then jumps back to the ingress edge and resumes. The Reset button also resets to the ingress edge rather than mid-transit. Previously the full orbit had to complete before the transit reappeared." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.5.0 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.5.0  —  2026-04-17" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• New Visualizer tab added between Parameters and Results. Displays a real-time animated transit simulation showing the planet crossing the stellar disk based on the current planet parameters (Rp/Rs, a/Rs, inclination, orbital period, mid-transit time). Animation updates automatically when parameters change." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Planet Parameters popup added to the Visualizer tab — click 'Edit Parameters' to open a detached window showing all planetary parameter fields for convenient reference and editing alongside the animation." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Revision History window added under the Help menu, replacing the inline notes in the About dialog." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Tab order updated: Data → Image Analysis → Parameters → Visualizer → Results → History." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.4.0 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.4.0  —  2026-04-16" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• App renamed to TransitLab. Title bar, About dialog, copyright line, and all user-facing strings updated." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Tab structure reorganised: the Observation tab has been dissolved. Directories (FITS, Save Plots, Darks, Flats, Biases) and the MicroObservatory section are now combined in a single Data tab. All remaining Observation fields (Observer Information, Observatory/Location, Plate Solve) are merged into the Parameters tab (formerly Equipment &amp; Target). Read FITS Header button is now at the top of the Parameters tab." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Tab order changed to: Data → Image Analysis → Parameters → Results → History." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Equipment layout compacted: Camera Type and Pixel Binning are now side by side; Latitude and Longitude are side by side; Filter Min and Max wavelengths are side by side; AAVSO and Secondary Observer Code fields each retain their own row." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Frame Analysis tab renamed to Image Analysis." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• 'Import Star List' renamed to 'Import NINA Star List'. The star list preview textbox has been removed — imported files still populate target and comp positions." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Frame flagging behaviour changed: scanning no longer automatically marks flagged frames as excluded. Frames are flagged (shown in status column) but exclusion requires an explicit action — either check Excl manually or click the new Auto-exclude Flagged button in the Image Analysis toolbar." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Save &amp; Run is now always clickable. If a new FITS directory has been browsed but Read FITS Header has not been clicked, a dialog explains the requirement and the run is blocked until the header is read." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• AAVSO comparison star fetch: when a NEA query is in progress and no planet coordinates are yet available, the comp fetch status now shows 'Waiting for NEA query to complete…' instead of an unhelpful no-comps message. The fetch proceeds automatically once the NEA query finishes." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• MObs: Cancel button added to the download controls. Clicking Cancel stops an in-progress file download." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• MObs: 'Use This Data' now stays on the Data tab rather than switching away." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• History: 'Download CSV' and 'Download XLSX' buttons renamed to 'Export CSV' and 'Export XLSX'." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• DataGrid backgrounds set to Transparent in Image Analysis and MObs observation list — empty row area below data no longer shows a distinct background block." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• About dialog: ASTAP (Astrometric STAcking Program) by Han Kleijn added to Acknowledgements." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• About dialog: release-of-liability disclaimer added after the copyright line." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Help menu: Quick Start guide added above User Guide — a concise 7-step walkthrough for new users." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Image Analysis: VSP controls (FOV, Mag, Star, VSP Chart) moved to a second row below the scan controls, freeing horizontal space and keeping the VSP Chart button fully visible." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Image Analysis: 'FOV′' label now shows the arcminute symbol directly after the label, not after the spinner." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Image Analysis: added 'Star:' text field next to the VSP controls. Resolves the catch-22 where the user had to read the FITS header before loading a VSP chart — the star name can now be typed directly. Auto-fills from NEA when data becomes available." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Image Analysis: 'x images flagged' counter added in the exclusion row. 'frames' renamed to 'images' throughout. Flagged counter shows in yellow when non-zero." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Image Analysis: VSP chart error window revised — no longer offers 'Open in Browser'. Instead shows a clear explanation that the star name was not recognised by AAVSO, with correction advice." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Image Analysis: VSP chart window changed from modal (ShowDialog) to non-modal (Show), so the app remains fully interactive while the chart is displayed." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Parameters tab: 'Obs. Elevation (meters)' label shortened to 'Elevation (meters)'. All fixed-width label columns changed to Auto-width so labels are never clipped." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Parameters tab: 'Import Star List' renamed to 'Import NINA Star List'." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Save &amp; Run: switches to the Results tab immediately after the header-read check passes, regardless of whether validation succeeds. Previously the switch only happened when EXOTIC actually launched." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Save &amp; Run: clicking the button while a new FITS directory has been browsed but the header not yet read now shows an explanatory dialog instead of silently doing nothing." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• DataGrid backgrounds set to Transparent in Image Analysis, MObs list, and History — eliminating the 'ghost' band below sparse data rows." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• TabControl background corrected from BrushBg2 to BrushBg — removes the visible tint between the tab header bar and tab content area." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• History button bar changed from WrapPanel to StackPanel — buttons no longer wrap to a second row at narrow widths." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Main window MinWidth increased to 1568 to match the default width and prevent toolbar elements from being clipped when the window is resized." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Restore Excluded redesigned: no longer opens a session-management dialog or moves files. Now simply un-checks all Excl boxes in the current image list. Excluded images are still physically moved aside before EXOTIC runs and restored automatically afterwards — no manual recovery is needed for normal use." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Exclusion session persistence removed: ExclusionSessions is no longer stored in config.json. The ExclusionSessionDialog is retired." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Two-stage confirm buttons (Delete Selected Files, Clear List) in the Restore Excluded dialog fixed: the button was disabled by the async relay command during the 4-second wait, making the second click impossible. Now synchronous with a background auto-reset timer." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Image Analysis Mag spinner width increased to prevent the value being clipped by the up-arrow." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• User Guide: Image Analysis section updated to reflect new flagging behaviour, Restore Excluded semantics, VSP Star field, and two-counter status row. Quick Start and About entries added to the Help menu description. Save &amp; Run FITS header requirement documented." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.3.3 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.3.3  —  2026-04-07" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Frame Analysis: manually unchecking a flagged frame's Excl checkbox now correctly preserves that choice through Save &amp; Run. Previously, any background operation that needed a FITS file path (plate solve, comp fetch, etc.) would silently re-check all flagged frames, overriding the user's exclusion choices." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• A confirmation dialog now appears when Save &amp; Run is clicked and one or more frames are marked for exclusion. The dialog lists each excluded frame by number and filename with Proceed and Cancel buttons. No dialog appears when no frames are excluded." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.3.2 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.3.2  —  2026-04-04" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Cancel now reliably stops EXOTIC even when it is waiting for a prompt response. Previously, if EXOTIC was in a calibration-directory prompt loop, the Cancel button had no effect because the prompt input was blocking the shutdown path." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Calibration directory prompts (Darks, Flats, Biases) are now answered automatically using the directories configured in the launcher, eliminating the prompt loop that occurred when EXOTIC could not find files at the path specified in inits.json. The alternate image extension prompt is also auto-answered 'n'." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Save Plots directory no longer stays locked to a manually-chosen location from a previous session. The auto-follow behaviour (Save Plots tracks the parent of the FITS directory) is now reset at the start of every session." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Clearing a calibration directory (Darks, Flats, or Biases) no longer displays the literal text 'null' in the field. The field is now correctly blanked and auto-detection resumes." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.3.1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.3.1  —  2026-04-02" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• NEA fetch: if Rp/Rs from the archive is outside the plausible range (0.01–0.35), it is now replaced by a value computed from transit depth or planet/stellar radii. The substituted Rp/Rs Uncertainty is propagated from the same source data; if no uncertainty data is available it is estimated at 10% of the substituted value." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• NEA fetch: a/Rs Uncertainty defaults to 0.1 when not reported by the archive." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• NEA fetch: Star Metallicity [Fe/H] defaults to 0.0 ± 0.1 (solar) when not reported by the archive." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• NEA fetch: a notification dialog now appears immediately after the fetch whenever any parameter was estimated (Rp/Rs substitution, a/Rs uncertainty default, metallicity default), listing exactly which values were changed. The user can review and edit before running EXOTIC." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Save &amp; Run: added pre-launch Rp/Rs sanity check — if the value in the field is outside 0.01–0.35 when Save &amp; Run is clicked, an error dialog is shown and the run is blocked until the value is corrected." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Read FITS Header now clears the Target Star X,Y field on every click, since pixel coordinates are image-specific and must be re-selected for each new session." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Observer code fields (AAVSO Code and Secondary Code) now populate immediately in the ComboBox after clicking Save, without requiring the user to re-select from the dropdown." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Frame Analysis: frames excluded counter now updates in real time when the Exc checkbox is toggled on any row." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• MObs: Download Selected now correctly downloads the selected observation after the list has been sorted by a column header. Previously, sorting the list caused the wrong observation to be downloaded." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• MObs: overnight observations whose files span midnight UTC are now grouped as a single observation. Previously, files timestamped after 00:00 UTC were split into a separate entry for the next calendar day." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• MObs: 'Set as default download folder' checkbox label corrected to 'Set as default download directory'." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• NEA status text now wraps instead of running off the right edge of the window for long status messages." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• ASTAP plate solve: 'Warning scale was inaccurate' is now correctly recognised as a successful solve — ASTAP detected the real FOV and scale from the image and wrote WCS to the file. Previously a display race condition caused this success case to appear as a failure." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• User Guide: new Section 10 — Plate Solve Setup — documents the Tools → Plate Solve Setup dialog, explains Astrometry.net vs ASTAP, and provides step-by-step ASTAP installation and configuration instructions." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• User Guide: search bar added at the top. Type any keyword and press Enter or click Find Next to cycle through all matching lines in the guide." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.3.0 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.3.0  —  2026-03-31" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Plate Solve Setup added under the Tools menu. The user can now choose between Astrometry.net (via EXOTIC, requires internet) and ASTAP (local, fast, no internet required) as the active plate solver. The selected solver is shown alongside the plate solve status on the Equipment &amp; Target tab." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• ASTAP settings: path to the ASTAP executable (with Browse and Auto-detect buttons), a Test button that verifies the installation and reports the version, and automatic catalog detection that warns if no star catalog (.1 files) is found in the ASTAP directory." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• ASTAP solve parameters: search radius (degrees, default 180) and downsample factor (default 0 = auto) are configurable in the setup dialog." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• When ASTAP is selected, EXOTIC is no longer required to perform a plate solve — the EXOTIC prerequisite check is skipped automatically." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.2.4 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.2.4  —  2026-03-31" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Python discovery extended to cover conda environments (miniconda3, anaconda3, and variants). If Python is not found via the standard installer locations or PATH, the launcher now locates exotic.exe in any conda env and derives python.exe from the same environment — eliminating 'Python not found' errors for users with conda-based EXOTIC installations." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Plate solve error message now includes the Python path when an import failure occurs, making environment mismatches easier to diagnose." Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• 'Python not found' error message updated to direct new users to the EXOTIC Setup tab rather than suggesting a settings path that doesn't apply on a fresh install." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.2.3 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.2.3  —  2026-03-30" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• AAVSO comparison star border and target-exclusion filters removed. All in-frame stars returned by the AAVSO VSP API are now passed directly to EXOTIC, restoring the original behavior. EXOTIC performs its own variability checks and best-comparison-star selection." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.2.2 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.2.2  —  2026-03-30" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• NEA query strategy updated to match EXOTIC's internal logic. The most recent publication from the per-publication table (ps, tran_flag=1) is now used as the primary data source, with earlier publications scanned for any remaining null fields. Previously, stellar parameters were filled from the composite parameters table (pscomppars), which can differ from what EXOTIC uses. This change further reduces parameter-difference prompts during a run."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Rp/Rs and a/Rs fallback calculations added: if the direct ratio is absent, Rp/Rs is computed from transit depth (ppm) or from planet/stellar radii; a/Rs is computed via Kepler's third law from the orbital period and stellar mass and radius. Missing inclination defaults to 90°, eccentricity to 0, and argument of periastron to 0 — matching EXOTIC's own fallbacks."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Frame Analysis: Filename column header is now clickable and sorts the file list. (Previously the column used a template that did not respond to header clicks.)"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• MObs: 'Set as default download folder' checkbox now persists across sessions. The Download Directory field and Browse button are disabled while the checkbox is checked, preventing accidental changes."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Save Plots Directory no longer resets when the FITS Files Directory is changed after the user has manually set a different Save Plots location."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Auto / Manual prompts toggle now shows a brief description of the active mode next to the switch."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• VSP Chart: the button now shows '⟳  Fetching chart…' and is disabled while the chart image is downloading. A Cancel button appears next to it during the fetch, allowing the request to be aborted if it takes too long."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Frame Analysis: 'Select All Flagged' button removed. Flagged frames are already excluded automatically when the scan completes, making the button redundant." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.2.1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.2.1  —  2026-03-28" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Auto Select Comps ranking changed from proximity-first to brightness-similarity (closest ADU match to target first). This naturally distributes comp stars across the frame rather than clustering them near the target — important for wide-pixel-scale setups such as MicroObservatory where nearby stars may overlap the target aperture."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Auto Select Comps minimum brightness floor lowered from 30% to 10% of target ADU, opening up more candidates in sparse fields while still excluding very faint, noisy stars."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• CV filter wavelength range corrected to 350–850 nm (was 400–700 nm) to match the actual broadband CCD response used by MicroObservatory and similar unfiltered setups." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.2.0 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.2.0  —  2026-03-27" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Auto / Manual prompts toggle: a toggle switch next to the EXOTIC Log label controls whether known EXOTIC prompts are answered automatically (Auto, default) or surfaced to the user (Manual). In Auto mode, secondary observer codes and the 'Enter 1 or 2' parameter-review prompt are answered silently. In Manual mode every EXOTIC question appears in the Results tab input box for the user to answer. Setting persists across sessions."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Comparison star selection improvements: AAVSO-fetched comp stars are now filtered for a 10% frame border margin and a 30-pixel target exclusion radius. Auto Select Comps updated: saturation limit is target ADU (no stars brighter than the target), minimum brightness floor at 30% of target ADU, target exclusion zone increased to 20-pixel radius, edge exclusion changed to 10% of frame dimensions, candidates ranked by proximity to target (closest first)."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Argument of Periastron defaults to 0 in inits.json when left blank, eliminating EXOTIC's 'omega is None' warning for circular/near-circular orbits."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Auto Select Comps now shows a pop-up dialog when 10 comparison stars are already selected." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.1.2 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.1.2  —  2026-03-27" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Interactive EXOTIC prompts: all questions EXOTIC asks during a run (NEA parameter differences, stellar parameter confirmations, coordinate mismatches) are now surfaced live in the Results tab. The user types a response and presses Enter or clicks Send — no more blind pre-fill of stdin."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• NEA query aligned with EXOTIC: NeaService now queries the default_flag=1 row (the same row EXOTIC uses) as the primary source. Stellar parameters absent from the default row are filled from the most recent publication. This eliminates the parameter-difference prompts in most runs."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Session fields cleared on exit: all status messages and parameter fields (planet params, stellar params, dates, coordinates, target/comp XY) are cleared when the app closes. Only directories and equipment defaults persist across sessions. Users must click Read FITS Header to begin a new session."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Save Plots Directory now defaults to the parent of the FITS Files Directory when the FITS dir is changed. Filter wavelength range (FilterMin/FilterMax) is auto-populated when Read FITS Header detects a known filter name (B, V, R, I, CV, SR, SI, etc.)."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Required-field validation: clicking Save &amp; Run with any required field empty now shows a modal error dialog listing every missing field at once, instead of silently doing nothing." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.1.1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.1.1  —  2026-03-27" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Status messages are now color-coded across all tabs: ✓ green (complete), ✗ red (failed), ⟳ / ⚠ yellow (in progress / warning). A global converter handles this automatically."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• MObs tab: column widths now auto-size to fit the longest content after data loads. Fixed the Avalonia DataGrid Width=Auto limitation by calculating explicit pixel widths in code."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• EXOTIC now adopts NASA Exoplanet Archive parameters by default when differences are found (option 2 — use Archive values). Previously the launcher's own values always took precedence."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• AAVSO comp fetch race condition fixed: clicking Read FITS Header no longer causes the comp fetch to fail immediately. The previous bug occurred when a concurrent NEA fetch cancelled the WCS fallback read before coordinates could be determined."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• VSP Chart now always opens in a popup window. Previously, a URL format issue caused the chart to open in the default browser instead."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Read FITS Header now waits for an in-progress frame scan to finish before reading the header. Previously it could return 'no non-excluded files found' if the scan was still running."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• EXOTIC Setup: Python installations are now validated by actually running Python (checks for a working interpreter), not just verifying the executable exists. Broken installs are now detected and flagged."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• EXOTIC Setup: EXOTIC status now resets correctly after a successful Python reinstall, clearing any stale 'Cannot check' message."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Menu bar labels are now 50% larger (FontSize 30) for better readability." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.1.0 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.1.0  —  2026-03-27" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• MObs tab: download science and calibration frames directly from the MicroObservatory telescope network (Cecilia, Donald, Ben, Ed). Lookback period, progress bar, and 'Use This Data' auto-populates FITS and Darks directories."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• EXOTIC Setup tab: automated wizard for installing Python 3.10.11 and EXOTIC on a new machine. Streams full pip output to a log box. Save Log button for diagnostics."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• History tab: permanent record of every AAVSO Exoplanet submission. Auto-populated after successful uploads. Columns: Planet, Obs, Date, Tmid ± uncertainty, (Rp/R*)² ± uncertainty, SNR, Depth, Inclination, Duration, Scatter. Export to CSV or XLSX; import from FinalParams JSON or prior export."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Instructions tab: built-in User Guide with table of contents and section navigation links."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Frame scan exclusion: a session dialog allows reviewing exclusions before EXOTIC runs; excluded files are physically moved to a sibling folder so EXOTIC cannot find them, and restored automatically after the run."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• NEA multi-row scan: NeaService now scans all publication rows in the composite parameters table and picks the first non-null value per field — Teff and other stellar parameters are reliably found even when absent from the most recent row."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• AAVSO Exoplanet (exosite) upload integrated directly into the Results tab. Confirmed upload is auto-recorded in History."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Observatory save/restore: saved observatories auto-match by lat/lon when loading a previous session." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v2.0.0 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v2.0.0  —  2026-03-11" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Full rewrite from Python / Tkinter to C# / Avalonia UI 11. Cross-platform (Windows and macOS)."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Core tabs: Observation, Equipment &amp; Target, Frame Analysis, Results."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Automatic plate solve via EXOTIC's PlateSolution API — triggered by Read FITS Header, no manual step required."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• AAVSO comparison stars fetched automatically once a WCS solution is available."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Planet parameters auto-fetched from NASA Exoplanet Archive when Read FITS Header populates the planet name."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Frame Analysis: background-based flagging with σ threshold; image viewer with stretch controls, histogram, zoom/pan, and target/comp star picking."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• VSP Chart viewer with configurable FOV and magnitude limit."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Recent Sessions menu: last 10 inits.json sessions for quick reload."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• EXOTIC runs embedded — output streamed live to the Results tab. Light curve displayed automatically when EXOTIC finishes." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

            <!-- ── v1.4.0 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <TextBlock Classes="h2" Text="v1.4.0  —  2026-03-22  (Python / Tkinter — final release)" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Last stable Python release. Built as a self-contained Windows executable via PyInstaller."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• All core reduction fields: directories, observer info, equipment, planet parameters."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• Automatic coordinate mismatch handling: pre-feeds 'n' to EXOTIC stdin so WCS coordinates are accepted without prompting."/>
            <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="• EXOTIC launched via conda environment scan (miniconda3/envs) with redirected stdout/stderr." Margin="0,0,0,12"/>

        </StackPanel>

    </ScrollViewer>

</UserControl>
